1
00:00:00,703 --> 00:00:03,333
(The Reason Behind Happiness)

2
00:00:03,473 --> 00:00:05,972
- It's nice to see you, everyone. - Nice to see you.

3
00:00:05,973 --> 00:00:07,942
My dear Sung Hwan, have you been well?

4
00:00:07,943 --> 00:00:09,072
- I've been well. - Gosh.

5
00:00:09,073 --> 00:00:11,113
Here's the thing. He hasn't been near our show...

6
00:00:11,383 --> 00:00:13,713
after losing the race to me last time. I guess he was upset.

7
00:00:14,113 --> 00:00:16,183
(He challenged Sung Hwan to a running race all of a sudden.)

8
00:00:16,483 --> 00:00:17,512
Go!

9
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:19,722
(The race took place in the middle of the night.)

10
00:00:19,723 --> 00:00:21,793
(In the end, Moomoo won the race.)

11
00:00:22,723 --> 00:00:24,723
(I have a cramp in my leg.)

12
00:00:24,893 --> 00:00:27,122
(Sung Hwan was only left with an excuse.)

13
00:00:27,123 --> 00:00:29,332
Well, I did get a cramp in my leg. That's the truth.

14
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:30,333
- So you lost. - Yes.

15
00:00:30,334 --> 00:00:31,832
- Yes, I lost. - You were so bad at running.

16
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,063
I lost. I know.

17
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:34,332
- I lost. - I thought you'd be good.

18
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:35,402
- No. - He was the worst.

19
00:00:35,403 --> 00:00:36,902
Listen. During the race,

20
00:00:36,903 --> 00:00:39,372
I tried to sprint at first. I have good upper body strength.

21
00:00:39,373 --> 00:00:40,743
- He had good upper body strength? - So when I was running,

22
00:00:40,843 --> 00:00:42,213
I got a cramp in my leg.

23
00:00:42,243 --> 00:00:43,472
Despite that, I ran 20m more...

24
00:00:43,473 --> 00:00:45,413
purely based on my mental strength. That's how we were tied.

25
00:00:45,513 --> 00:00:46,742
- I see. - Oh, my.

26
00:00:46,743 --> 00:00:49,312
Is it necessary to review the race in such detail?

27
00:00:49,313 --> 00:00:50,313
The thing is...

28
00:00:50,314 --> 00:00:51,652
(Chuckling)

29
00:00:51,653 --> 00:00:52,722
It's like he's being chased.

30
00:00:52,723 --> 00:00:54,893
- His glasses are steaming up. - Right.

31
00:00:54,993 --> 00:00:56,422
- No. They aren't steaming up. - Are you already hot?

32
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:58,122
- This is... - Are you crying, Sung Hwan?

33
00:00:58,123 --> 00:00:59,293
They're getting misty.

34
00:00:59,663 --> 00:01:01,192
You know what? Let's do it again...

35
00:01:01,193 --> 00:01:02,432
- once my leg cramp is gone. - Let's do it now.

36
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:03,562
- When will that happen exactly? - Let's do it whenever.

37
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:06,203
Then let's hold a sports day.

38
00:01:06,463 --> 00:01:08,202
We can make your race the main event of the sports day.

39
00:01:08,203 --> 00:01:09,732
But making that the main event sounds ridiculous.

40
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:10,902
- This is the main event? - Right?

41
00:01:10,903 --> 00:01:13,402
Since we're on the subject, you and I...

42
00:01:13,403 --> 00:01:15,272
- should have a go at it. - Then let's do this.

43
00:01:15,273 --> 00:01:16,842
- Do what? - We'll divide into...

44
00:01:16,843 --> 00:01:18,482
- Team Sung Hwan and Team Hyun Moo. - Okay.

45
00:01:18,483 --> 00:01:19,483
Team Moo and Team Ku.

46
00:01:19,484 --> 00:01:20,642
I'll join Team Hyun Moo then.

47
00:01:20,643 --> 00:01:21,783
- Same here. - Me too.

48
00:01:23,113 --> 00:01:25,482
(Team Moo, not Team Ku?)

49
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:26,782
Hold on.

50
00:01:26,783 --> 00:01:28,052
Who knew I'd be their first pick?

51
00:01:28,053 --> 00:01:29,092
- Hold on. - I want to be on Team Hyun Moo.

52
00:01:29,093 --> 00:01:30,093
- Me too. - Okay.

53
00:01:30,094 --> 00:01:31,222
Okay. Let's do this then.

54
00:01:31,223 --> 00:01:32,762
- I'll prepare myself for it. - Gosh, challenge me whenever.

55
00:01:32,763 --> 00:01:35,432
Sure. I've got nothing to worry about.

56
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:37,092
- You know what? Something crazy... - Yes.

57
00:01:37,093 --> 00:01:39,633
Happened during the weekend.

58
00:01:39,803 --> 00:01:41,573
I'm serious when I say this.

59
00:01:41,873 --> 00:01:45,142
He's one of my cherished stars I hold dear to my heart.

60
00:01:45,143 --> 00:01:46,173
You mean SAN?

61
00:01:46,643 --> 00:01:48,513
(Na Rae has recently been hooked on...)

62
00:01:48,613 --> 00:01:50,273
(the K-pop group, ATEEZ.)

63
00:01:51,313 --> 00:01:56,013
(And her favorite star is SAN.)

64
00:01:56,383 --> 00:01:58,153
(I want my sweethearts to be happy.)

65
00:01:58,483 --> 00:02:00,353
(A few days later, on Hyun Moo's social media)

66
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:01,522
- Gosh. - Hello.

67
00:02:01,523 --> 00:02:02,952
- Hong Joong. - Hello.

68
00:02:02,953 --> 00:02:04,393
- SAN. - Hello.

69
00:02:04,523 --> 00:02:06,322
(The greeting from the man Na Rae is into)

70
00:02:06,323 --> 00:02:07,462
(What is this? What? He's my favorite!)

71
00:02:07,463 --> 00:02:09,393
(Na Rae was furious after watching the clip.)

72
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:11,432
- You have never... - Right.

73
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:12,962
Mentioned ATEEZ or even so much as their music.

74
00:02:12,963 --> 00:02:14,333
- Why did you go there? - Right.

75
00:02:14,703 --> 00:02:15,703
He posted the clip almost right away.

76
00:02:15,704 --> 00:02:18,272
That's the only hobby I have. Why did you have to take it from me?

77
00:02:18,273 --> 00:02:19,643
But SAN is mine.

78
00:02:19,773 --> 00:02:20,803
What...

79
00:02:21,003 --> 00:02:22,743
Na Rae, I'll sing their song at karaoke.

80
00:02:22,973 --> 00:02:24,142
No!

81
00:02:24,143 --> 00:02:25,543
How about Kian84 instead of SAN?

82
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:28,612
(He will perform for only one person.)

83
00:02:28,613 --> 00:02:29,953
I'll sing their song.

84
00:02:31,683 --> 00:02:33,553
Anyway, I brought something from Japan.

85
00:02:33,883 --> 00:02:34,923
- What? - What?

86
00:02:35,053 --> 00:02:36,522
- He must've brought a present. - He must've brought a souvenir.

87
00:02:36,523 --> 00:02:38,262
My gosh. I knew you'd be furious.

88
00:02:38,263 --> 00:02:40,022
So I got you a present despite my busy schedule.

89
00:02:40,023 --> 00:02:41,293
- What is it? - You know? Here.

90
00:02:41,763 --> 00:02:44,933
This is their merchandise shirt. It's the same design SAN wore.

91
00:02:45,163 --> 00:02:47,332
It's ATEEZ's shirt. I got him to sign the shirt.

92
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,033
- My gosh. Really? - Here.

93
00:02:49,273 --> 00:02:50,372
- Thank you. - Exactly.

94
00:02:50,373 --> 00:02:52,042
- Thank you. - You can't even find this online...

95
00:02:52,043 --> 00:02:53,272
- because the design is sold out. - Yes.

96
00:02:53,273 --> 00:02:54,373
- Check the back. - Hold on.

97
00:02:54,913 --> 00:02:56,112
(Carefully checking the shirt not to damage it)

98
00:02:56,113 --> 00:02:57,872
- Let's see. - Gosh. Are you that happy?

99
00:02:57,873 --> 00:03:00,113
- Hold on. There it is. - It's there.

100
00:03:00,213 --> 00:03:01,242
There it is.

101
00:03:01,243 --> 00:03:02,312
- "To Na Rae. - "Na Rae."

102
00:03:02,313 --> 00:03:04,652
"Na Rae, I'm always grateful."

103
00:03:04,653 --> 00:03:06,123
- "Have a good day." - Yes.

104
00:03:06,253 --> 00:03:07,622
- Gosh. - I'll forever be loyal to you.

105
00:03:07,623 --> 00:03:08,922
- You're not upset now. Right? - Yes.

106
00:03:08,923 --> 00:03:10,752
- I went there to get you this. - I'm sorry.

107
00:03:10,753 --> 00:03:12,022
- He's indeed Fathermoo. - For you,

108
00:03:12,023 --> 00:03:13,292
I'd give up a kidney.

109
00:03:13,293 --> 00:03:14,423
(Feeling proud)

110
00:03:15,133 --> 00:03:18,532
(More Joy in Being Together)

111
00:03:18,533 --> 00:03:19,663
The weather is great.

112
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:24,232
(Going somewhere with a bag, full of bread)

113
00:03:24,233 --> 00:03:26,443
(It's Ju Seung.)

114
00:03:27,343 --> 00:03:29,073
(In a good mood)

115
00:03:31,343 --> 00:03:34,413
(I've arrived!)

116
00:03:36,683 --> 00:03:37,783
All right.

117
00:03:37,983 --> 00:03:39,182
(He naturally grabs the package.)

118
00:03:39,183 --> 00:03:40,983
- Isn't that his mother's house? - Right. Isn't that his mom's house?

119
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:44,222
My goodness.

120
00:03:44,223 --> 00:03:45,423
(Opening up)

121
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:48,092
Come back in, Coco.

122
00:03:48,093 --> 00:03:49,733
- Come in. Yes. - It's Coco.

123
00:03:49,833 --> 00:03:50,862
Come back in, Coco.

124
00:03:50,863 --> 00:03:52,402
(Ju Seung visits his mother's house and is welcomed by Coco.)

125
00:03:52,403 --> 00:03:53,802
- We've gotten close. - Yes, you have.

126
00:03:53,803 --> 00:03:55,333
- She's wagging her tail. - Is Ju Seung here?

127
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:57,173
Who is it? Is it your brother or sister?

128
00:03:57,403 --> 00:03:59,203
- Come on in. - It's your brother. Come on in.

129
00:03:59,443 --> 00:04:00,473
Come in.

130
00:04:00,703 --> 00:04:02,343
- You've gotten very close. - Yes.

131
00:04:02,813 --> 00:04:03,813
(Happy to see Coco)

132
00:04:04,343 --> 00:04:05,513
- You got a package. - Put it there.

133
00:04:07,143 --> 00:04:08,883
- That's your brother. - It's your brother.

134
00:04:09,283 --> 00:04:10,413
Is it from the online shopping mall?

135
00:04:10,983 --> 00:04:13,423
(He runs a restaurant in Vietnam.)

136
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:15,493
(Ju Seung's brother, Ju Ang)

137
00:04:16,293 --> 00:04:17,523
- Where's my sister-in-law? - Give it to me.

138
00:04:17,993 --> 00:04:18,993
Your sister-in-law?

139
00:04:18,994 --> 00:04:20,492
- Did she come with him? - I bought some bread.

140
00:04:20,493 --> 00:04:22,063
- It was supposed to come yesterday. - Bread?

141
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,332
- Bread... Hello. - Hello, Ju Seung.

142
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:25,503
- My gosh. - What?

143
00:04:25,663 --> 00:04:26,832
- My gosh. - I see.

144
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:28,333
- That's your sister-in-law. - Hello, Ju Seung.

145
00:04:28,703 --> 00:04:31,433
- She's so beautiful. - Oh, my.

146
00:04:33,303 --> 00:04:34,542
Why did you buy so much bread?

147
00:04:34,543 --> 00:04:36,243
A new bakery opened up in the neighborhood.

148
00:04:37,213 --> 00:04:38,513
Gosh, it tastes great.

149
00:04:38,843 --> 00:04:39,942
It tastes great?

150
00:04:39,943 --> 00:04:41,243
(There's a wide array of tasty bread.)

151
00:04:41,883 --> 00:04:43,783
- She's not fluent in Korean yet. - Right.

152
00:04:44,213 --> 00:04:45,652
My sister-in-law's name is...

153
00:04:45,653 --> 00:04:49,823
Nguyen Thi Minh Thu. That's her name.

154
00:04:49,853 --> 00:04:51,293
They had their wedding...

155
00:04:51,923 --> 00:04:54,323
in Vietnam last September.

156
00:04:55,333 --> 00:04:56,592
After being married for a year,

157
00:04:56,593 --> 00:05:00,132
they had their second wedding in Korea.

158
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,402
- The wedding was a week ago. - A week?

159
00:05:01,403 --> 00:05:03,932
- It just happened then. - They came to Korea together...

160
00:05:03,933 --> 00:05:06,543
- to have the wedding here. - Yes. It was for the wedding.

161
00:05:06,643 --> 00:05:08,412
Did they have the wedding at the venue you checked out?

162
00:05:08,413 --> 00:05:10,143
- They did. - They had it at that venue?

163
00:05:10,673 --> 00:05:11,882
(The venue was selected carefully...)

164
00:05:11,883 --> 00:05:13,213
(after his thorough inspection.)

165
00:05:14,043 --> 00:05:15,652
Yes. You were half crazy that day.

166
00:05:15,653 --> 00:05:16,913
- The ruler maniac. - You measured everything.

167
00:05:17,853 --> 00:05:19,983
(They match.)

168
00:05:20,853 --> 00:05:22,393
(I approve of this venue.)

169
00:05:23,523 --> 00:05:24,992
(At the venue he approved of...)

170
00:05:24,993 --> 00:05:26,393
The venue looks great.

171
00:05:26,763 --> 00:05:28,792
- It's the perfect height. - Nice. You chose a great venue.

172
00:05:28,793 --> 00:05:31,493
My sister-in-law was so happy with the venue. I felt so proud.

173
00:05:32,663 --> 00:05:34,162
Sung Hwan was the MC.

174
00:05:34,163 --> 00:05:35,733
- You were the MC? - I was.

175
00:05:36,173 --> 00:05:38,643
He's in limelight with everything he does lately.

176
00:05:39,143 --> 00:05:40,643
That'd be me. Nice to meet you. I'm Actor Ku Sung Hwan.

177
00:05:41,173 --> 00:05:42,773
- Gosh. - He said that to introduce himself.

178
00:05:43,413 --> 00:05:45,112
Other people are supposed to say that about him.

179
00:05:45,113 --> 00:05:46,613
(Feeling shy)

180
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:48,953
- So... Yes. - I was the MC at the wedding.

181
00:05:49,213 --> 00:05:51,583
"Groom Lee Ju Ang."

182
00:05:51,753 --> 00:05:52,822
- "Bride..." - Nguyen.

183
00:05:52,823 --> 00:05:53,823
I couldn't say her name.

184
00:05:53,824 --> 00:05:55,422
- It was her full name. - I had to say her full name.

185
00:05:55,423 --> 00:05:57,922
Nguyen is her family name. Minh Thu is her name.

186
00:05:57,923 --> 00:06:00,022
Minh means smart and clever.

187
00:06:00,023 --> 00:06:01,363
Thu means autumn.

188
00:06:01,893 --> 00:06:03,232
- Smart autumn. - Minh Thu.

189
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:04,833
- Smart autumn. - Smart autumn.

190
00:06:04,933 --> 00:06:06,463
- Ju Ang, do you want water? - Yes.

191
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:09,103
- Ju Seung, do you want water? - Thank you.

192
00:06:09,873 --> 00:06:11,033
She's so cute.

193
00:06:12,003 --> 00:06:14,203
I just washed my hands. Do you want some?

194
00:06:15,513 --> 00:06:16,713
It's nice to see her...

195
00:06:18,313 --> 00:06:19,313
in the video.

196
00:06:20,043 --> 00:06:22,413
My gosh. His mother is smiling at her like a proud mom.

197
00:06:23,313 --> 00:06:24,652
You know what?

198
00:06:24,653 --> 00:06:26,252
- They seem happier together. - Yes.

199
00:06:26,253 --> 00:06:27,253
- Right. - I can definitely see the change.

200
00:06:27,254 --> 00:06:28,822
The atmosphere change after a wedding in the family.

201
00:06:28,823 --> 00:06:30,093
You guys seem much happier.

202
00:06:30,553 --> 00:06:31,723
Did you eat?

203
00:06:31,923 --> 00:06:33,522
- A little bit earlier. - She's hungry.

204
00:06:33,523 --> 00:06:34,763
He's still hungry.

205
00:06:35,033 --> 00:06:36,392
I guess you like to eat in small bits,

206
00:06:36,393 --> 00:06:37,732
- but multiple times. - Yes.

207
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:39,702
- In small bits? - She's from Vietnam.

208
00:06:39,703 --> 00:06:40,962
She might not understand that.

209
00:06:40,963 --> 00:06:42,133
Enjoy.

210
00:06:42,733 --> 00:06:44,533
(She tears a small bit of the food and eats it.)

211
00:06:45,543 --> 00:06:47,503
(They enjoy the bread together as a family.)

212
00:06:48,003 --> 00:06:49,112
(Salivating)

213
00:06:49,113 --> 00:06:50,243
Look at Coco.

214
00:06:50,843 --> 00:06:53,143
Have you been well since the wedding?

215
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:55,552
We drove her parents to the airport today.

216
00:06:55,553 --> 00:06:58,053
- I see. They left today. Right. - I see.

217
00:06:58,253 --> 00:06:59,723
The wedding was quite hectic, wasn't it?

218
00:07:00,123 --> 00:07:01,993
A bit. It was hectic.

219
00:07:02,193 --> 00:07:05,122
My mother-in-law didn't speak Korean at all.

220
00:07:05,123 --> 00:07:06,693
- Not even a word. - You took care of her.

221
00:07:07,123 --> 00:07:08,833
It was her first time traveling abroad.

222
00:07:09,093 --> 00:07:10,932
She had never been on a plane before our wedding.

223
00:07:10,933 --> 00:07:12,663
- Gosh, she must've been so happy. - Really?

224
00:07:13,063 --> 00:07:15,272
- Then she must've been happy. - This is big.

225
00:07:15,273 --> 00:07:16,332
- She must've been. - Yes.

226
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:17,833
- She was happy. - She loved her trip.

227
00:07:18,173 --> 00:07:20,902
She had Korean food for the first time too.

228
00:07:20,903 --> 00:07:22,043
I see.

229
00:07:22,273 --> 00:07:23,772
- So... - Where have you visited...

230
00:07:23,773 --> 00:07:25,342
during your trip here? Have you been traveling a lot?

231
00:07:25,343 --> 00:07:26,613
I've been to...

232
00:07:27,443 --> 00:07:28,513
Jeju Island.

233
00:07:28,613 --> 00:07:29,613
- Gosh. - Jeju Island.

234
00:07:29,614 --> 00:07:30,912
- Suwon. - Suwon?

235
00:07:30,913 --> 00:07:32,052
- Suwon. - Songdo, Incheon.

236
00:07:32,053 --> 00:07:33,622
- How did she go there? - Songdo, Incheon.

237
00:07:33,623 --> 00:07:35,052
Yes. I've been to Yangyang.

238
00:07:35,053 --> 00:07:36,422
- Yangyang. - Yangyang.

239
00:07:36,423 --> 00:07:37,923
I've been to the downtown area.

240
00:07:38,023 --> 00:07:39,722
- The downtown area. - By that...

241
00:07:39,723 --> 00:07:40,922
- Downtown? - Hongdae.

242
00:07:40,923 --> 00:07:42,233
- Hongdae. Myeong-dong. - Myeong-dong.

243
00:07:42,363 --> 00:07:43,432
- Sinchon. - Sinchon.

244
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:45,303
- She's been to many places. - Sinchon.

245
00:07:45,333 --> 00:07:47,302
So she's been to popular places...

246
00:07:47,303 --> 00:07:50,303
she saw on social media.

247
00:07:50,703 --> 00:07:52,743
Of course, she must want to visit all these places.

248
00:07:52,903 --> 00:07:54,302
Will you have dinner too?

249
00:07:54,303 --> 00:07:56,213
- We should. - Okay.

250
00:07:56,743 --> 00:07:58,583
- Have fun. - Okay.

251
00:07:59,283 --> 00:08:00,413
Come home early.

252
00:08:01,043 --> 00:08:02,352
I'll be home around 7pm.

253
00:08:02,353 --> 00:08:04,453
- Come home early. - I'll be home around 7pm or 8pm.

254
00:08:04,683 --> 00:08:05,782
Where's he going?

255
00:08:05,783 --> 00:08:07,622
He said he had to wrap up some work stuff...

256
00:08:07,623 --> 00:08:09,252
before heading back to Vietnam.

257
00:08:09,253 --> 00:08:11,762
I decided to be her guide today.

258
00:08:11,763 --> 00:08:13,593
- It's been a while. - Businessmen have a lot of work.

259
00:08:13,723 --> 00:08:15,563
On a day like today,

260
00:08:15,663 --> 00:08:18,332
your brother must've felt awful because...

261
00:08:18,333 --> 00:08:20,002
- she would've been home alone. - Right.

262
00:08:20,003 --> 00:08:23,272
But having Ju Seung as her guide would be lovely.

263
00:08:23,273 --> 00:08:24,672
I hope Ju Seung did a good job as her guide.

264
00:08:24,673 --> 00:08:25,673
(Worried)

265
00:08:25,674 --> 00:08:27,043
That's the problem.

266
00:08:27,403 --> 00:08:28,842
- Let's go. - Yes.

267
00:08:28,843 --> 00:08:30,313
We have to get going right about now.

268
00:08:30,613 --> 00:08:31,783
- Let's go. - Okay.

269
00:08:32,213 --> 00:08:33,943
- Coco, I'll be back soon. - Okay.

270
00:08:34,343 --> 00:08:36,082
I'm heading out first.

271
00:08:36,083 --> 00:08:38,183
- Bye. - All right.

272
00:08:39,123 --> 00:08:40,423
I'll be back, Coco.

273
00:08:41,183 --> 00:08:43,193
- Are you ready? - Yes, I'm ready.

274
00:08:44,053 --> 00:08:45,363
(Fixing her hair)

275
00:08:45,963 --> 00:08:47,422
(They fix each other's clothes.)

276
00:08:47,423 --> 00:08:48,433
- Gosh. - Oh, my.

277
00:08:49,033 --> 00:08:51,233
- Their outfits look similar. - Right. You know what?

278
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:53,362
They seem to be getting along very well.

279
00:08:53,363 --> 00:08:54,663
Does this not work with this outfit?

280
00:08:56,133 --> 00:08:57,872
- Does it look weird? - So weird.

281
00:08:57,873 --> 00:08:59,672
(Playful)

282
00:08:59,673 --> 00:09:01,072
Whenever she comes to Korea,

283
00:09:01,073 --> 00:09:03,642
she stays with my mom for over ten days.

284
00:09:03,643 --> 00:09:06,142
So naturally, they've become quite close.

285
00:09:06,143 --> 00:09:07,712
- That's nice. - It's wonderful.

286
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:09,982
His mother treats her like her own.

287
00:09:09,983 --> 00:09:10,983
- I see. - Right.

288
00:09:10,984 --> 00:09:12,683
So Thu feels comfortable around her.

289
00:09:12,883 --> 00:09:15,253
But this one is loose on my head.

290
00:09:15,523 --> 00:09:17,793
This is the perfect color, but it'd look weird when I put it on.

291
00:09:18,423 --> 00:09:19,562
Is this better? Should I wear this?

292
00:09:19,563 --> 00:09:21,163
I know that this color is a good match.

293
00:09:21,293 --> 00:09:22,762
- Sure. - It suits the outfit the best.

294
00:09:22,763 --> 00:09:24,163
- It suits the outfit the best? Yes. - Yes.

295
00:09:24,963 --> 00:09:26,733
All right. Let's go. Bye, Coco.

296
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:28,332
Bye, Coco.

297
00:09:28,333 --> 00:09:29,502
- Three. - Let's go.

298
00:09:29,503 --> 00:09:31,333
- Let's go. - Let's go.

299
00:09:32,543 --> 00:09:34,403
(Dashing away)

300
00:09:34,773 --> 00:09:36,072
I'll be back, Coco.

301
00:09:36,073 --> 00:09:37,772
You know what? Coco goes to her room...

302
00:09:37,773 --> 00:09:39,383
when she knows we're leaving.

303
00:09:39,743 --> 00:09:41,113
- She knows they're leaving. - Yes.

304
00:09:41,713 --> 00:09:43,452
Actually, Coco might be happy that they're leaving.

305
00:09:43,453 --> 00:09:44,453
(I have the house to myself.)

306
00:09:44,454 --> 00:09:45,983
- She needs to regroup too. - Right.

307
00:09:47,983 --> 00:09:49,392
She's been to so many places already.

308
00:09:49,393 --> 00:09:50,752
- Where could you take her to? - Right.

309
00:09:50,753 --> 00:09:52,293
I had a lot on my mind.

310
00:09:52,923 --> 00:09:55,793
- Thu, your wedding in Vietnam... - Yes.

311
00:09:56,233 --> 00:09:58,533
Was it last year or two years ago? I can't even remember.

312
00:09:58,863 --> 00:10:01,203
Time flies by.

313
00:10:02,103 --> 00:10:03,472
Has it been a year?

314
00:10:03,473 --> 00:10:07,043
Which wedding did you like more? The one in Vietnam? Or in Korea?

315
00:10:07,143 --> 00:10:08,643
- I liked the one in Korea. - What?

316
00:10:09,173 --> 00:10:10,713
My makeup looked beautiful.

317
00:10:10,913 --> 00:10:12,713
- My dress was beautiful. - Yes.

318
00:10:13,043 --> 00:10:14,943
- So... Right. - It was all bling bling.

319
00:10:15,683 --> 00:10:18,212
I researched everything for the wedding in great detail.

320
00:10:18,213 --> 00:10:19,322
I even measured the height...

321
00:10:19,323 --> 00:10:20,422
- of the platform. - Him and the platform height.

322
00:10:20,423 --> 00:10:22,493
You liked it, right?

323
00:10:23,393 --> 00:10:26,293
Thank you so much, Ju Seung.

324
00:10:28,223 --> 00:10:31,093
Thank you so much, Ju Seung.

325
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:34,033
I guess you asked her multiple times already.

326
00:10:34,503 --> 00:10:36,132
- Right. - I asked her about three times.

327
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:37,302
That's a lot indeed.

328
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:38,473
Vietnamese has distinctive tones.

329
00:10:38,743 --> 00:10:41,403
Right. She's speaking Korean like she's speaking Vietnamese.

330
00:10:41,743 --> 00:10:44,673
Thank you so much, Ju Seung.

331
00:10:47,843 --> 00:10:50,013
Did you study Korean for a year?

332
00:10:50,953 --> 00:10:51,983
Five months.

333
00:10:52,053 --> 00:10:53,183
- Five months? - Yes.

334
00:10:53,553 --> 00:10:55,293
Then your Korean improved quite fast.

335
00:10:55,453 --> 00:10:57,693
She spoke much better Korean compared to last year.

336
00:10:58,023 --> 00:10:59,522
My Japanese isn't improving at all.

337
00:10:59,523 --> 00:11:01,022
How can her Korean improve that fast?

338
00:11:01,023 --> 00:11:02,863
- Kian84, what's monkey in Japanese? - Monkey.

339
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:04,063
"Saru."

340
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:07,162
That's all I know.

341
00:11:07,163 --> 00:11:08,363
(I got my self-esteem back.)

342
00:11:09,433 --> 00:11:11,103
How long have you been with my brother?

343
00:11:11,633 --> 00:11:13,302
How long have you been with my brother?

344
00:11:13,303 --> 00:11:14,672
- Three years. - Three years?

345
00:11:14,673 --> 00:11:15,673
Yes, three years.

346
00:11:15,674 --> 00:11:17,443
Three years. So you dated for two years.

347
00:11:17,643 --> 00:11:19,143
- Yes. - Then you got married in Vietnam...

348
00:11:19,243 --> 00:11:21,213
- and in Korea after 1 year. - After 1 year... Yes.

349
00:11:22,013 --> 00:11:23,913
Is my brother good to you?

350
00:11:24,153 --> 00:11:25,953
He's so good to me.

351
00:11:26,223 --> 00:11:27,323
What does he do for you?

352
00:11:27,823 --> 00:11:29,323
Ju Ang is...

353
00:11:30,493 --> 00:11:31,653
just nice to me.

354
00:11:32,093 --> 00:11:34,123
He doesn't cheat on me. I hate that the most.

355
00:11:34,993 --> 00:11:37,593
- That's the most important quality. - This is the most important.

356
00:11:38,133 --> 00:11:39,203
He doesn't gamble.

357
00:11:39,603 --> 00:11:40,702
- He doesn't gamble. - Right.

358
00:11:40,703 --> 00:11:42,203
So it's because he doesn't do problematic things.

359
00:11:42,903 --> 00:11:44,002
- You must be in love... - He just doesn't cause problems.

360
00:11:44,003 --> 00:11:45,072
- to learn a language. - Right.

361
00:11:45,073 --> 00:11:46,903
- Dating can help a lot. - That's true.

362
00:11:47,243 --> 00:11:48,403
His shape is pretty.

363
00:11:49,273 --> 00:11:50,943
- His shape is pretty. - His shape is pretty?

364
00:11:51,143 --> 00:11:52,343
- Doesn't she mean he's handsome? - His shape is pretty.

365
00:11:53,013 --> 00:11:54,742
- His shape... - You mean his face?

366
00:11:54,743 --> 00:11:55,813
Yes. His face.

367
00:11:56,153 --> 00:11:57,783
She's saying your brother is handsome.

368
00:11:58,683 --> 00:12:00,322
- He's handsome. - His appearance.

369
00:12:00,323 --> 00:12:01,323
(Hearing about his brother's secret for the first time)

370
00:12:03,893 --> 00:12:04,953
Where are you going, by the way?

371
00:12:06,163 --> 00:12:07,463
We'll be there in ten minutes.

372
00:12:09,193 --> 00:12:10,732
(Korean Folk Village)

373
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:11,762
(Spotting it)

374
00:12:11,763 --> 00:12:12,963
- Korean Folk Village? - I see.

375
00:12:13,403 --> 00:12:14,962
Since she's in Korea,

376
00:12:14,963 --> 00:12:16,573
she ought to visit the Korean Folk Village.

377
00:12:17,003 --> 00:12:20,103
My sister-in-law hasn't been to the Korean Folk Village yet.

378
00:12:20,603 --> 00:12:23,043
The first spot I took her to was the Korean Folk Village.

379
00:12:23,673 --> 00:12:24,843
The name says it over there, Thu.

380
00:12:25,313 --> 00:12:27,043
- Gyeonggi Province... Over there. - Where? I see.

381
00:12:27,243 --> 00:12:29,352
"Korean Folk Village."

382
00:12:29,353 --> 00:12:30,813
- It's 500m away. - Yes, Korean Folk Village.

383
00:12:31,053 --> 00:12:32,752
- She can read everything. - You're good at reading too.

384
00:12:32,753 --> 00:12:34,023
Could you read what's on the bottom too?

385
00:12:34,853 --> 00:12:35,953
- Where? - The one on the bottom.

386
00:12:36,223 --> 00:12:38,763
"Gyeonggi Arts Center."

387
00:12:40,223 --> 00:12:42,763
Who's that? Someone is doing a concert here.

388
00:12:43,893 --> 00:12:45,262
- Read the big letters. - Choi Baek Ho.

389
00:12:45,263 --> 00:12:46,563
- What? - Choi Baek Ho.

390
00:12:47,303 --> 00:12:48,462
(Choi Baek Ho)

391
00:12:48,463 --> 00:12:49,703
She can read it.

392
00:12:50,373 --> 00:12:52,702
- He's the symbol of romance. - Gosh, I'd love to go to that.

393
00:12:52,703 --> 00:12:53,773
- He's amazing. - Right.

394
00:12:54,373 --> 00:12:56,712
(With romance in the air...)

395
00:12:56,713 --> 00:12:57,872
We've arrived.

396
00:12:57,873 --> 00:12:58,883
(they arrive at the Korean Folk Village.)

397
00:12:59,943 --> 00:13:00,983
(Opening the door)

398
00:13:01,543 --> 00:13:02,912
Gosh, it's so sunny.

399
00:13:02,913 --> 00:13:03,913
(Walking in the warm sunshine)

400
00:13:04,913 --> 00:13:06,053
How are you feeling?

401
00:13:06,653 --> 00:13:08,282
(Holding hands)

402
00:13:08,283 --> 00:13:09,292
They seem so close.

403
00:13:09,293 --> 00:13:10,352
They look like a mom and a daughter.

404
00:13:10,353 --> 00:13:11,422
Right.

405
00:13:11,423 --> 00:13:14,193
By the way, it looks like you two coordinated the outfits today.

406
00:13:14,323 --> 00:13:15,693
No, we didn't.

407
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:19,133
Both of your outfits are in the color of autumn leaves.

408
00:13:19,933 --> 00:13:21,433
This is the only outfit I have.

409
00:13:21,733 --> 00:13:22,833
(Right?)

410
00:13:23,033 --> 00:13:25,173
I want to wear an outfit in floral pink...

411
00:13:25,573 --> 00:13:26,902
- Later... - or rose pink.

412
00:13:26,903 --> 00:13:28,173
- Rose pink. - I want to wear pink outfits too.

413
00:13:28,273 --> 00:13:29,443
But I don't have any.

414
00:13:30,813 --> 00:13:32,642
- Come on. - "Buy me one."

415
00:13:32,643 --> 00:13:34,482
She wants to go to a department store, Ju Seung.

416
00:13:34,483 --> 00:13:35,712
Why are you pretending not to hear her?

417
00:13:35,713 --> 00:13:36,952
I have a hard time picking up on that.

418
00:13:36,953 --> 00:13:38,112
- Why is that? - That's hard for me.

419
00:13:38,113 --> 00:13:39,452
I thought they were talking to each other.

420
00:13:39,453 --> 00:13:41,883
Have you ever held hands when you were out with your mom?

421
00:13:42,053 --> 00:13:44,022
- Have you held her hand? - Gosh, sons don't do that.

422
00:13:44,023 --> 00:13:45,662
- Have you done that? - What do you think?

423
00:13:45,663 --> 00:13:47,663
(Me?)

424
00:13:48,893 --> 00:13:51,133
I guess we have to buy the tickets here.

425
00:13:52,303 --> 00:13:54,133
- We have to buy a ticket? - Yes.

426
00:13:54,303 --> 00:13:55,373
Will you buy it?

427
00:13:57,033 --> 00:13:58,132
He'll take care of it.

428
00:13:58,133 --> 00:13:59,273
- He will? - Don't worry about that.

429
00:14:00,203 --> 00:14:01,843
We have to use the kiosk for the tickets.

430
00:14:02,943 --> 00:14:04,643
This is the one. We must use the kiosk.

431
00:14:04,773 --> 00:14:06,283
Stay there. It's hot here.

432
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:09,382
You're doing a proper job as their guide.

433
00:14:09,383 --> 00:14:10,753
(Buying the tickets)

434
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:12,323
This tree looks beautiful.

435
00:14:12,723 --> 00:14:14,753
Yes. That's a beautiful color. It's so green.

436
00:14:15,323 --> 00:14:16,453
Isn't your bag heavy, Mother?

437
00:14:16,823 --> 00:14:18,123
It's not heavy.

438
00:14:18,493 --> 00:14:20,063
Is yours heavy? Should we use the parasol?

439
00:14:20,163 --> 00:14:21,792
- The parasol? Let's use it later. - It's way too hot.

440
00:14:21,793 --> 00:14:23,433
She's good to your mother too.

441
00:14:24,763 --> 00:14:26,063
- Hello. - Hello.

442
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:27,962
- Three people. - Welcome.

443
00:14:27,963 --> 00:14:29,733
- Hello. Thank you. - Thank you.

444
00:14:30,873 --> 00:14:32,242
It's the Korean Folk Village.

445
00:14:32,243 --> 00:14:34,243
(He prepared this itinerary for a unique experience.)

446
00:14:35,203 --> 00:14:36,342
There were so many foreigners.

447
00:14:36,343 --> 00:14:37,712
Especially after "KPop Demon Hunters" premiered.

448
00:14:37,713 --> 00:14:38,713
(Packed with tourists from all over the world)

449
00:14:39,043 --> 00:14:41,243
Even the zoomers go to the Korean Folk Village these days.

450
00:14:42,183 --> 00:14:45,553
To feel closer to a country, one has to learn about its history.

451
00:14:45,653 --> 00:14:47,153
That's the process of getting to know a country.

452
00:14:47,453 --> 00:14:49,453
As her guide for the day,

453
00:14:49,593 --> 00:14:52,092
I'll take her to traditional places,

454
00:14:52,093 --> 00:14:54,693
- so we can make memories together. - That's nice.

455
00:14:55,763 --> 00:14:58,233
- There are many performances too. - The village has a lot of programs.

456
00:15:00,363 --> 00:15:03,333
We must go to the Fabric Dye Street. Let's go to Section 14.

457
00:15:04,373 --> 00:15:06,143
- This should be our route. - Where is it?

458
00:15:06,303 --> 00:15:07,903
That way, we won't have to go around twice.

459
00:15:08,543 --> 00:15:09,713
Let's go straight.

460
00:15:10,673 --> 00:15:12,743
(Guide Ju leads them while checking the map.)

461
00:15:13,743 --> 00:15:15,883
Is it a slow day here because it's a weekday?

462
00:15:16,453 --> 00:15:18,953
Mother, did people make kimchi with that?

463
00:15:19,053 --> 00:15:21,122
- People still store it in there. - They do?

464
00:15:21,123 --> 00:15:22,553
- I see. Jangdokdae. - I see.

465
00:15:22,923 --> 00:15:24,023
(Intrigued)

466
00:15:24,223 --> 00:15:25,663
I saw that in many dramas.

467
00:15:26,593 --> 00:15:28,793
- It's a thatched roof house. - That?

468
00:15:29,863 --> 00:15:31,332
A thatched roof house.

469
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:32,732
When I was young,

470
00:15:32,733 --> 00:15:34,532
I had houses like this in my neighborhood.

471
00:15:34,533 --> 00:15:36,632
- Did you live in a house like this? - My house...

472
00:15:36,633 --> 00:15:38,733
No. I used to live in a big house.

473
00:15:40,803 --> 00:15:42,443
Houses used to look like this back in the day.

474
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:44,743
That's how spoons used to look back then.

475
00:15:45,113 --> 00:15:46,543
Spoons improved over the years.

476
00:15:46,643 --> 00:15:47,743
Spoons.

477
00:15:48,783 --> 00:15:50,213
This is fascinating for her.

478
00:15:51,213 --> 00:15:52,983
(Checking)

479
00:15:53,183 --> 00:15:54,183
(He leads them while diligently studying the map.)

480
00:15:54,184 --> 00:15:56,723
(Following)

481
00:15:57,653 --> 00:15:59,693
We've reached the administrative office now.

482
00:16:00,363 --> 00:16:01,992
(Guide Ju enters the office well ahead of them.)

483
00:16:01,993 --> 00:16:03,732
You should walk with them. Why...

484
00:16:03,733 --> 00:16:04,833
He's their guide.

485
00:16:05,163 --> 00:16:07,033
He must feel impatient. He's in a hurry.

486
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:09,172
- Right. He wants it to be perfect. - Yes.

487
00:16:09,173 --> 00:16:10,173
(His passion as their guide makes him walk faster.)

488
00:16:11,173 --> 00:16:13,473
- Have you seen this in a drama? - In a drama?

489
00:16:13,543 --> 00:16:15,443
- And he sounds manly today too. - Yes.

490
00:16:15,713 --> 00:16:17,213
When you commit a crime,

491
00:16:17,973 --> 00:16:19,282
- they... - They twist your legs there.

492
00:16:19,283 --> 00:16:20,783
- Twisting the legs? - This is what happens.

493
00:16:21,443 --> 00:16:22,852
(Demonstrating how one's legs get twisted)

494
00:16:22,853 --> 00:16:24,082
- Have you not seen this? - I have.

495
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:27,122
- I've watched it in a Korean drama. - Back then, there was no evidence.

496
00:16:27,123 --> 00:16:28,353
They couldn't take pictures.

497
00:16:28,483 --> 00:16:30,523
They made criminals confess by this punishment.

498
00:16:30,793 --> 00:16:31,952
This is where the punishment took place.

499
00:16:31,953 --> 00:16:33,622
And the district magistrate would be sitting over there.

500
00:16:33,623 --> 00:16:34,823
You're trying your best.

501
00:16:34,993 --> 00:16:36,992
I've watched this in dramas.

502
00:16:36,993 --> 00:16:38,832
Shouldn't you take a picture in the magistrate chair?

503
00:16:38,833 --> 00:16:39,833
Not anyone could sit there.

504
00:16:39,834 --> 00:16:41,133
If we were in the Joseon Era, you would've been punished.

505
00:16:42,473 --> 00:16:44,832
(She goes to the magistrate chair as instructed by the guide.)

506
00:16:44,833 --> 00:16:46,142
Listen up.

507
00:16:46,143 --> 00:16:47,573
One, two, three.

508
00:16:48,003 --> 00:16:49,413
Come here.

509
00:16:49,773 --> 00:16:51,042
Listen up.

510
00:16:51,043 --> 00:16:52,282
One, two, three.

511
00:16:52,283 --> 00:16:53,443
Say, "Listen up."

512
00:16:54,883 --> 00:16:56,853
What should I do, Mother?

513
00:16:57,113 --> 00:16:58,983
- They get along so well together. - Right.

514
00:16:59,153 --> 00:17:00,883
(Taking pictures of them enjoying the magistrate chair)

515
00:17:01,523 --> 00:17:02,822
- This is funny. - What?

516
00:17:02,823 --> 00:17:03,893
This is funny.

517
00:17:04,453 --> 00:17:07,792
(After they finish looking around the administrative office, )

518
00:17:07,793 --> 00:17:09,633
(he checks the pamphlet again.)

519
00:17:11,593 --> 00:17:13,233
We need to go this way to reach the photo spot.

520
00:17:14,303 --> 00:17:15,433
If we go this way...

521
00:17:16,973 --> 00:17:18,103
This is it.

522
00:17:18,603 --> 00:17:19,703
Wanhyangroo.

523
00:17:19,873 --> 00:17:21,003
Wanhyangroo?

524
00:17:21,743 --> 00:17:22,973
I bet it will be cool in here.

525
00:17:23,373 --> 00:17:24,643
There's a lake here too.

526
00:17:26,713 --> 00:17:28,913
(Wanhyangroo)

527
00:17:29,153 --> 00:17:31,982
You know, aristocrats used to sing for entertainment.

528
00:17:31,983 --> 00:17:33,453
This was the place of their entertainment.

529
00:17:33,853 --> 00:17:34,952
(A nugak that offers a glimpse into the ancestors' taste for arts)

530
00:17:34,953 --> 00:17:36,523
You explained it in easy terms.

531
00:17:36,793 --> 00:17:38,022
She didn't know the details.

532
00:17:38,023 --> 00:17:40,022
So I only explained simple things while we were there.

533
00:17:40,023 --> 00:17:41,163
- I see. - I see. Okay.

534
00:17:43,793 --> 00:17:47,533
(They get closer to the nugak, following the tune.)

535
00:17:49,103 --> 00:17:50,402
There are so many foreigners.

536
00:17:50,403 --> 00:17:53,003
(There are so many foreigners.)

537
00:17:53,203 --> 00:17:54,203
(Wanhyangroo is filled with visitors.)

538
00:17:54,204 --> 00:17:55,542
- Is there a performance? - Luckily, we went in...

539
00:17:55,543 --> 00:17:56,842
when they were performing.

540
00:17:56,843 --> 00:17:58,673
Great. This is excellent.

541
00:18:03,353 --> 00:18:04,553
(Taking pictures)

542
00:18:05,013 --> 00:18:06,252
(Guide Ju takes pictures of them during the performance.)

543
00:18:06,253 --> 00:18:07,523
You're taking pictures of them in the back.

544
00:18:08,423 --> 00:18:12,523
(A picture of them enjoying the performance)

545
00:18:13,793 --> 00:18:16,393
(Engrossed in the performance, clueless of what he's doing)

546
00:18:19,903 --> 00:18:20,963
That's cool.

547
00:18:23,473 --> 00:18:24,533
That's a carp.

548
00:18:25,473 --> 00:18:26,673
A fish?

549
00:18:26,743 --> 00:18:28,743
That's a carp. It's a fish.

550
00:18:29,213 --> 00:18:31,473
- There's a big one too. - A big one?

551
00:18:31,913 --> 00:18:33,442
- This is the photo spot. - What?

552
00:18:33,443 --> 00:18:34,482
- Let's take pictures here. - Here?

553
00:18:34,483 --> 00:18:36,083
In the end, pictures are what last.

554
00:18:36,453 --> 00:18:38,012
- Why don't you take one together? - Let's take one together.

555
00:18:38,013 --> 00:18:39,183
Together.

556
00:18:40,523 --> 00:18:41,623
- Make a heart. - I'll take it.

557
00:18:41,723 --> 00:18:42,893
- One, two, three. - How?

558
00:18:43,893 --> 00:18:45,763
- Oh, how lovely this is. - Yes, what a lovely sight.

559
00:18:49,363 --> 00:18:51,063
Stand there, and I'll take a picture of you.

560
00:18:52,163 --> 00:18:53,533
- I see. - By herself?

561
00:18:54,863 --> 00:18:56,633
I don't know how to pose for it.

562
00:18:57,233 --> 00:18:58,372
(An awkward pose)

563
00:18:58,373 --> 00:18:59,802
Come this way.

564
00:18:59,803 --> 00:19:01,943
(He tells her where to stand as she feels shy.)

565
00:19:02,843 --> 00:19:04,973
One.

566
00:19:09,053 --> 00:19:11,212
(An impressive change in her facial expression)

567
00:19:11,213 --> 00:19:12,282
- Hold on. - At last.

568
00:19:12,283 --> 00:19:15,483
- Hold on. Is she an influencer? - At last.

569
00:19:15,993 --> 00:19:17,122
She's not an influencer?

570
00:19:17,123 --> 00:19:19,093
There's finally someone who can understand me.

571
00:19:21,293 --> 00:19:22,393
One.

572
00:19:22,733 --> 00:19:23,892
Did you see her breathing technique?

573
00:19:23,893 --> 00:19:25,033
- She held her breath. - Yes.

574
00:19:25,393 --> 00:19:26,402
(KEY became someone else in front of a camera.)

575
00:19:26,403 --> 00:19:27,532
Why...

576
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:28,632
That way, you'll look natural...

577
00:19:28,633 --> 00:19:30,102
- in the photos. - Check out her gaze and shoulders.

578
00:19:30,103 --> 00:19:31,533
(She's as classy as an idol star.)

579
00:19:31,803 --> 00:19:32,973
- She looks captivating. - Yes.

580
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,803
One more time. Pull out your hand.

581
00:19:36,513 --> 00:19:37,843
She's really not an influencer?

582
00:19:38,013 --> 00:19:39,142
- No. - I see.

583
00:19:39,143 --> 00:19:40,913
She just loves having her pictures taken.

584
00:19:42,953 --> 00:19:44,352
(Busy)

585
00:19:44,353 --> 00:19:46,022
- Right here. - Here?

586
00:19:46,023 --> 00:19:48,053
- Does it look pretty? - One, two, three.

587
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:51,693
(She doesn't leave her hands alone for a moment.)

588
00:19:51,793 --> 00:19:54,163
I could tell that she had experience posing in front of cameras.

589
00:19:54,293 --> 00:19:55,932
There's a video that went viral.

590
00:19:55,933 --> 00:19:59,403
She turned her fingers while posing for cameras.

591
00:19:59,533 --> 00:20:00,533
This?

592
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:02,602
- Yes, I know. - Yes.

593
00:20:02,603 --> 00:20:04,172
It's like she's a Living National Treasure...

594
00:20:04,173 --> 00:20:05,303
when it comes to posing for cameras.

595
00:20:05,533 --> 00:20:07,343
My brother told me that...

596
00:20:07,403 --> 00:20:09,713
on a daily basis, she usually takes...

597
00:20:09,843 --> 00:20:11,273
about 500 to 1,000 pictures.

598
00:20:11,773 --> 00:20:13,742
(She's serious about taking pictures.)

599
00:20:13,743 --> 00:20:16,183
- She looks beautiful. Oh, my. - My gosh.

600
00:20:17,913 --> 00:20:19,823
Having her pictures taken is her only hobby.

601
00:20:19,923 --> 00:20:22,592
When they got married in Vietnam,

602
00:20:22,593 --> 00:20:24,493
my brother's eyes were almost out of focus...

603
00:20:24,593 --> 00:20:26,323
because they took so many pictures.

604
00:20:26,723 --> 00:20:27,963
This is why!

605
00:20:28,093 --> 00:20:30,493
Look at the picture. He was holding his phone that day.

606
00:20:30,663 --> 00:20:31,932
- Look. - My gosh!

607
00:20:31,933 --> 00:20:33,002
(A tight grip)

608
00:20:33,003 --> 00:20:35,202
- Grooms don't usually carry phones. - He was holding his phone.

609
00:20:35,203 --> 00:20:36,932
- You're so sharp! - Yes.

610
00:20:36,933 --> 00:20:38,372
Seriously. He's so sharp.

611
00:20:38,373 --> 00:20:39,443
(Exactly, my point.)

612
00:20:39,473 --> 00:20:42,373
I've never seen a groom holding a phone at his own wedding.

613
00:20:42,513 --> 00:20:44,912
I found out that she really loved being photographed.

614
00:20:44,913 --> 00:20:47,642
I thought that we should do something she'd enjoy the most.

615
00:20:47,643 --> 00:20:49,152
That's why I took them to a place...

616
00:20:49,153 --> 00:20:51,153
- with a lot of photo spots. - That's great.

617
00:20:51,253 --> 00:20:53,023
Our show has Mootographer.

618
00:20:53,153 --> 00:20:55,182
But just for today, I'm Jutographer.

619
00:20:55,183 --> 00:20:56,252
He's stealing Hyun Moo's thing.

620
00:20:56,253 --> 00:20:57,892
- Gosh, he can't steal that from me. - What?

621
00:20:57,893 --> 00:20:59,122
It's about time I took it from him.

622
00:20:59,123 --> 00:21:00,793
I don't consider phone cameras as real cameras.

623
00:21:01,823 --> 00:21:02,863
(Clicking)

624
00:21:03,793 --> 00:21:05,192
I'm Jutographer.

625
00:21:05,193 --> 00:21:06,402
(I'm Jutographer.)

626
00:21:06,403 --> 00:21:07,863
- Click. - That's a different pose.

627
00:21:08,803 --> 00:21:09,903
My gosh.

628
00:21:10,133 --> 00:21:11,673
(Jutographer is at work.)

629
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:13,472
(She showcases a variety of poses like the Living National Treasure.)

630
00:21:13,473 --> 00:21:15,243
- Gosh, Minh Thu is so cool. - Oh, my.

631
00:21:15,813 --> 00:21:17,572
(I'm determined to take great pictures.)

632
00:21:17,573 --> 00:21:18,613
That's giving me the creeps.

633
00:21:20,283 --> 00:21:21,312
One, two, three.

634
00:21:21,313 --> 00:21:22,313
(He spreads out his legs to take her pictures.)

635
00:21:22,314 --> 00:21:23,553
You look like a pro.

636
00:21:23,653 --> 00:21:27,583
(Jutographer doesn't stop taking pictures.)

637
00:21:28,253 --> 00:21:29,293
How do they look?

638
00:21:29,723 --> 00:21:30,753
How do they look?

639
00:21:30,923 --> 00:21:32,193
- She's checking them right away. - She's checking them right away.

640
00:21:32,963 --> 00:21:34,663
(What do you think?)

641
00:21:34,823 --> 00:21:37,033
Gosh, you're good.

642
00:21:37,533 --> 00:21:38,933
- Did they come out well? - They look great.

643
00:21:39,563 --> 00:21:40,932
(His sister-in-law loves the pictures.)

644
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:42,032
It looks a bit blurry.

645
00:21:42,033 --> 00:21:44,172
- You should've wiped the lens. - Right. You should have.

646
00:21:44,173 --> 00:21:45,872
No, this degree of blurriness is fine.

647
00:21:45,873 --> 00:21:48,072
Aligning the water at her waist level...

648
00:21:48,073 --> 00:21:49,213
makes her legs look longer.

649
00:21:49,743 --> 00:21:51,642
- That's good. It's a nice photo. - I can't align it at her neck.

650
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:52,743
- Okay. - You've got some skills.

651
00:21:54,883 --> 00:21:56,453
They look great.

652
00:21:56,883 --> 00:21:59,113
- You're good. - Yes.

653
00:22:00,053 --> 00:22:01,083
Okay.

654
00:22:02,653 --> 00:22:04,223
(I'm proud of you, Jutographer.)

655
00:22:04,553 --> 00:22:05,893
Next...

656
00:22:08,323 --> 00:22:11,193
(Looking around to find the next spot)

657
00:22:12,093 --> 00:22:13,503
This place is beautiful too.

658
00:22:13,803 --> 00:22:15,262
What's that? Is it a tombstone?

659
00:22:15,263 --> 00:22:16,333
Let's take one here.

660
00:22:16,503 --> 00:22:18,073
Yes. This tree is beautiful.

661
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:20,242
Could you stand over there? Let me take pictures of you.

662
00:22:20,243 --> 00:22:22,773
When I spotted good lighting for pictures,

663
00:22:23,013 --> 00:22:24,313
- I took pictures of her right away. - Gosh.

664
00:22:24,913 --> 00:22:26,243
Here? How?

665
00:22:27,143 --> 00:22:29,043
(Feeling shy again)

666
00:22:29,413 --> 00:22:30,853
I'll let the light flow in.

667
00:22:30,913 --> 00:22:32,083
One, two, three.

668
00:22:32,213 --> 00:22:34,583
(Her gaze changing)

669
00:22:34,923 --> 00:22:35,952
(Feeling proud)

670
00:22:35,953 --> 00:22:38,723
I can't align that at your neck. Hold on. From here...

671
00:22:39,323 --> 00:22:40,992
One, two, three.

672
00:22:40,993 --> 00:22:42,362
- Gosh. She's a natural. - One, two, three.

673
00:22:42,363 --> 00:22:43,463
Okay.

674
00:22:44,793 --> 00:22:47,232
- It will adjust the lighting soon. - But...

675
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:48,333
See? It's adjusting the lighting.

676
00:22:48,603 --> 00:22:50,232
I love that kind of lighting in my photos.

677
00:22:50,233 --> 00:22:51,403
You can see it partially.

678
00:22:51,603 --> 00:22:52,603
Doesn't it look great?

679
00:22:52,703 --> 00:22:53,703
It looks awful.

680
00:22:54,343 --> 00:22:55,773
I'm glad if you don't like it.

681
00:22:55,843 --> 00:22:57,572
- I like it. - You take good pictures.

682
00:22:57,573 --> 00:22:59,143
Why are your pictures all tilted?

683
00:22:59,243 --> 00:23:01,643
- AI can fix the alignment. - AI can do it.

684
00:23:02,413 --> 00:23:04,352
I used the pro mode.

685
00:23:04,353 --> 00:23:05,353
Doesn't it look good?

686
00:23:05,354 --> 00:23:06,483
You're a good photographer.

687
00:23:07,853 --> 00:23:09,553
- Even she's taking pictures. - She's walking too.

688
00:23:10,623 --> 00:23:13,323
(The photo shoot with professionals continue.)

689
00:23:15,793 --> 00:23:17,863
- Should we sit down for a bit? - Let's take a break.

690
00:23:18,733 --> 00:23:20,833
(They take a short break after taking tons of pictures.)

691
00:23:21,533 --> 00:23:23,173
Mother, do you want to go to the restroom?

692
00:23:23,473 --> 00:23:25,032
- Do you want to go? - Sure. I should use it too.

693
00:23:25,033 --> 00:23:26,103
- The restroom? - Yes.

694
00:23:26,473 --> 00:23:28,003
It's fun to go to the restroom together.

695
00:23:29,003 --> 00:23:31,043
(Jutographer is left all alone.)

696
00:23:31,113 --> 00:23:32,113
Oh, my legs.

697
00:23:32,114 --> 00:23:34,083
(Sprawled out)

698
00:23:35,183 --> 00:23:37,152
- Gosh, he must be tired. - Yes.

699
00:23:37,153 --> 00:23:38,283
(Let me take a short break.)

700
00:23:39,883 --> 00:23:41,522
(Closing his eyes)

701
00:23:41,523 --> 00:23:43,753
- Did you really doze off? - Yes, because it was breezy there.

702
00:23:44,153 --> 00:23:45,422
If you dozed off,

703
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:46,693
- they were gone for a while then. - Yes.

704
00:23:52,633 --> 00:23:53,963
What's taking them so long?

705
00:23:54,963 --> 00:23:57,233
I guess they abandoned you and left without you.

706
00:23:58,233 --> 00:23:59,403
I almost fell asleep.

707
00:24:02,603 --> 00:24:04,013
There they are.

708
00:24:04,073 --> 00:24:05,173
They're coming back.

709
00:24:06,313 --> 00:24:07,783
- What? - What?

710
00:24:07,913 --> 00:24:08,913
What?

711
00:24:08,914 --> 00:24:10,183
- Did she change her outfit? - She changed her outfit.

712
00:24:10,783 --> 00:24:11,783
What?

713
00:24:12,213 --> 00:24:13,553
Did you change your outfit?

714
00:24:15,723 --> 00:24:18,053
Yes, because we're taking pictures.

715
00:24:18,223 --> 00:24:20,192
- For pictures? - For pictures.

716
00:24:20,193 --> 00:24:22,733
She always carries several outfits...

717
00:24:23,063 --> 00:24:25,232
- in the trunk of her car. - Really?

718
00:24:25,233 --> 00:24:27,633
She's always ready to change her outfit.

719
00:24:28,233 --> 00:24:30,102
For Minh Thu, this is an international trip.

720
00:24:30,103 --> 00:24:31,602
- Right, it is. - Yes, it is.

721
00:24:31,603 --> 00:24:32,672
- She's never been here before. - Right.

722
00:24:32,673 --> 00:24:34,502
- Of course. - She must want to dress up for it.

723
00:24:34,503 --> 00:24:36,472
I can totally understand. She belongs to my club.

724
00:24:36,473 --> 00:24:38,112
It's like her photo shoot as the broom-to-be.

725
00:24:38,113 --> 00:24:39,143
Right, the dress.

726
00:24:40,243 --> 00:24:43,513
(A heavy suitcase is inevitable for photo maniacs.)

727
00:24:44,253 --> 00:24:45,753
You look beautiful.

728
00:24:45,983 --> 00:24:47,123
Is it heavy?

729
00:24:47,253 --> 00:24:48,322
(She walks out confidently to score the best pictures.)

730
00:24:48,323 --> 00:24:50,093
- She's serious about pictures. - Thank you.

731
00:24:50,223 --> 00:24:51,553
For real.

732
00:24:52,493 --> 00:24:54,323
(From the matching beige outfit with her mother-in-law...)

733
00:24:54,963 --> 00:24:56,632
(to a bright pink outfit)

734
00:24:56,633 --> 00:24:58,892
- She brought another pair of shoes? - Of course.

735
00:24:58,893 --> 00:25:00,703
(She changes her style from head to toe.)

736
00:25:01,633 --> 00:25:03,602
(Amazed)

737
00:25:03,603 --> 00:25:04,773
You seem sick of it.

738
00:25:05,003 --> 00:25:06,773
- That's why you took so long. - Where should we take pictures?

739
00:25:07,643 --> 00:25:09,572
- I'll take one for you. - With Mother?

740
00:25:09,573 --> 00:25:11,143
- You go ahead. Do it without me. - Let's take one by yourself.

741
00:25:11,513 --> 00:25:12,982
- My mother... - Yes.

742
00:25:12,983 --> 00:25:14,583
Hates taking pictures.

743
00:25:15,283 --> 00:25:17,553
(He starts taking pictures with two phones.)

744
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:19,453
You're taking pictures with two different phones?

745
00:25:19,853 --> 00:25:20,982
Two, three.

746
00:25:20,983 --> 00:25:23,593
(Jutographer records memories of his new family member.)

747
00:25:25,123 --> 00:25:26,363
Over there. Yes.

748
00:25:27,193 --> 00:25:28,463
These pictures look great.

749
00:25:30,433 --> 00:25:31,633
I think they came out well.

750
00:25:33,133 --> 00:25:34,563
Gosh, you're good.

751
00:25:35,433 --> 00:25:37,073
- Do you like them? - "You're good."

752
00:25:37,733 --> 00:25:39,333
- Pictures here look great. - Yes.

753
00:25:39,503 --> 00:25:41,203
Yes. The colors really pop. How beautiful.

754
00:25:42,913 --> 00:25:44,572
If you don't like them, I can take them again.

755
00:25:44,573 --> 00:25:45,973
- I like them. Yes. - You do?

756
00:25:46,513 --> 00:25:48,883
(Showing off the pictures to her mother-in-law)

757
00:25:49,583 --> 00:25:51,883
The pink outfit looks better in pictures.

758
00:25:52,283 --> 00:25:53,322
Let me take a picture of you.

759
00:25:53,323 --> 00:25:54,423
- Her too? - My gosh.

760
00:25:55,353 --> 00:25:57,152
(Striking up a pretty pose in front of her mother-in-law)

761
00:25:57,153 --> 00:25:58,653
- You're helping her make memories. - Yes.

762
00:26:00,363 --> 00:26:02,063
Your mother likes taking pictures of her too.

763
00:26:02,763 --> 00:26:04,593
She never had a daughter.

764
00:26:05,533 --> 00:26:08,003
- You're always smiling. - This spot looks great.

765
00:26:08,833 --> 00:26:11,973
(He keeps snapping photos wherever they go.)

766
00:26:12,403 --> 00:26:15,843
It looks like your brother fabricated a fake meeting.

767
00:26:16,643 --> 00:26:17,943
(Stuttering)

768
00:26:18,143 --> 00:26:19,943
(Ju Ang didn't sound sure of himself.)

769
00:26:20,183 --> 00:26:21,513
I think he left on purpose.

770
00:26:21,713 --> 00:26:22,852
He wanted a break?

771
00:26:22,853 --> 00:26:24,213
Did he go to the hospital to get his thumb checked out?

772
00:26:24,783 --> 00:26:26,323
Maybe, his thumbprint faded away.

773
00:26:26,823 --> 00:26:28,753
I bet his phone is always heated.

774
00:26:28,953 --> 00:26:30,023
Did you take a lot of pictures?

775
00:26:30,193 --> 00:26:31,353
I snapped about 40 pictures.

