through Instagram.

1888
01:08:06,043 --> 01:08:07,843
"Ku Sung Hwan's family came to have a meal."

1889
01:08:08,043 --> 01:08:10,142
"They only ate the food and left."

1890
01:08:10,143 --> 01:08:11,242
Oh, without talking?

1891
01:08:11,243 --> 01:08:13,052
Like a gourmet club?

1892
01:08:13,053 --> 01:08:16,053
- You're like a foodie crew. - They really are.

1893
01:08:17,353 --> 01:08:19,793
(They came out to Dongsung-ro after making memories.)

1894
01:08:20,153 --> 01:08:22,423
There's the underground mall if you go down here.

1895
01:08:23,723 --> 01:08:25,763
- This is the bookstore, right? - Yes.

1896
01:08:26,293 --> 01:08:27,462
I remember this place.

1897
01:08:27,463 --> 01:08:28,833
Why did I come here so often?

1898
01:08:29,463 --> 01:08:32,633
Here? Didn't you come here to buy music albums?

1899
01:08:34,603 --> 01:08:35,972
I used to collect CD albums.

1900
01:08:35,973 --> 01:08:37,142
I bought all of them there.

1901
01:08:37,143 --> 01:08:38,373
(Young Ki Bum went there to buy CD albums.)

1902
01:08:39,873 --> 01:08:42,342
- Cassette tapes and CDs. - That's right.

1903
01:08:42,343 --> 01:08:44,082
- You came here to buy them. - You're right.

1904
01:08:44,083 --> 01:08:45,382
- You always came here for those. - How long has it been...

1905
01:08:45,383 --> 01:08:46,713
since you last went there?

1906
01:08:47,053 --> 01:08:49,052
Last time I went there was when I was 16.

1907
01:08:49,053 --> 01:08:51,152
- It's been really long. - There was no occasion to go there.

1908
01:08:51,153 --> 01:08:52,292
That's right.

1909
01:08:52,293 --> 01:08:53,652
I just went there to rest.

1910
01:08:53,653 --> 01:08:55,423
- To look around. - There are many things to do there.

1911
01:08:55,663 --> 01:08:57,663
Right. This is how it looked.

1912
01:08:58,593 --> 01:09:00,063
- You remember this? - Yes.

1913
01:09:00,693 --> 01:09:02,263
This is the underground mall.

1914
01:09:02,703 --> 01:09:04,933
- The mall is still here. - Of course.

1915
01:09:05,533 --> 01:09:06,872
It's just that there aren't many customers now.

1916
01:09:06,873 --> 01:09:08,042
Oh, thank you.

1917
01:09:08,043 --> 01:09:09,343
(Will it look the same?)

1918
01:09:11,543 --> 01:09:14,473
- This place is huge. - It is big. It's always been big.

1919
01:09:16,283 --> 01:09:17,482
(Packed with various stationery and items)

1920
01:09:17,483 --> 01:09:18,782
Time goes by really quickly...

1921
01:09:18,783 --> 01:09:20,513
- when you have some time to kill. - That's right.

1922
01:09:21,953 --> 01:09:23,853
My mom loves stationery.

1923
01:09:24,653 --> 01:09:26,123
- She keeps a journal too. - She keeps a journal.

1924
01:09:27,453 --> 01:09:30,493
(Parenting journal is a must.)

1925
01:09:31,563 --> 01:09:35,502
(KEY's mother still keeps a journal.)

1926
01:09:35,503 --> 01:09:36,632
She still writes a journal?

1927
01:09:36,633 --> 01:09:38,103
Why do you look so young there?

1928
01:09:38,973 --> 01:09:40,902
(Bitter)

1929
01:09:40,903 --> 01:09:41,942
- Kian84. - Kian84.

1930
01:09:41,943 --> 01:09:43,042
- My gosh. - I don't think...

1931
01:09:43,043 --> 01:09:44,142
you should do a marathon.

1932
01:09:44,143 --> 01:09:46,942
- It's the aftereffect, for sure. - You shouldn't run too much.

1933
01:09:46,943 --> 01:09:49,212
- You're right. - That wasn't so long ago.

1934
01:09:49,213 --> 01:09:50,942
- It isn't. - It's only three years ago.

1935
01:09:50,943 --> 01:09:52,982
You have a fair face and thick hair.

1936
01:09:52,983 --> 01:09:55,623
Does running make you age fast?

1937
01:09:55,723 --> 01:09:57,823
- I was surprised too. - Oh, my.

1938
01:09:58,823 --> 01:09:59,852
It's cute.

1939
01:09:59,853 --> 01:10:01,963
This is cute. Wallace and Gromit.

1940
01:10:02,263 --> 01:10:04,123
- This looks good. - People use keyrings a lot.

1941
01:10:05,063 --> 01:10:06,932
- Who cares? - This one's nice.

1942
01:10:06,933 --> 01:10:07,933
(Grabbing one as soon as she sees it)

1943
01:10:08,263 --> 01:10:09,363
You should get one too.

1944
01:10:09,633 --> 01:10:11,772
Yes, she'd pick one at ease at times like this.

1945
01:10:11,773 --> 01:10:13,402
I used to love stationery...

1946
01:10:13,403 --> 01:10:14,972
- when I was young. - I love it too.

1947
01:10:14,973 --> 01:10:17,472
- Really? - You can't help but take after her.

1948
01:10:17,473 --> 01:10:19,242
- Because she loves it... - A daughter-like son.

1949
01:10:19,243 --> 01:10:20,912
Oh, really?

1950
01:10:20,913 --> 01:10:23,283
- I still love it. - Me too.

1951
01:10:24,913 --> 01:10:26,683
I love things like this. Cards.

1952
01:10:27,183 --> 01:10:29,553
- You like maximal stuff. - Yes.

1953
01:10:29,753 --> 01:10:32,222
Your mother has the same taste as mine.

1954
01:10:32,223 --> 01:10:33,552
- She likes fully decorated ones. - This one's nice too.

1955
01:10:33,553 --> 01:10:35,763
- Get one each. - A girlish sentiment.

1956
01:10:36,123 --> 01:10:39,333
Gosh, it's a diary for ten years.

1957
01:10:40,133 --> 01:10:41,193
Do you want to get one?

1958
01:10:41,563 --> 01:10:42,632
Do you think...

1959
01:10:42,633 --> 01:10:43,662
- you can keep it for a year? - Of course.

1960
01:10:43,663 --> 01:10:45,473
- Your mom would. - You have to write it every day.

1961
01:10:45,973 --> 01:10:47,602
- I write it every day already. - She's already written it...

1962
01:10:47,603 --> 01:10:48,603
over ten years.

1963
01:10:48,604 --> 01:10:50,243
- Get one. - You should get one for her.

1964
01:10:50,503 --> 01:10:51,872
I'll get this.

1965
01:10:51,873 --> 01:10:53,442
It was not popular...

1966
01:10:53,443 --> 01:10:55,382
- that it was 70 percent off. - Of course.

1967
01:10:55,383 --> 01:10:56,442
People don't write a lot these days.

1968
01:10:56,443 --> 01:10:58,112
Most people don't dare buy it.

1969
01:10:58,113 --> 01:10:59,552
- A journal for ten years is... - But my mom...

1970
01:10:59,553 --> 01:11:01,182
My gosh. My mom loved it...

1971
01:11:01,183 --> 01:11:03,222
- as soon as she saw it. - People don't write these days.

1972
01:11:03,223 --> 01:11:06,253
- Right, let alone journals. - It suited my mom's taste the most.

1973
01:11:06,693 --> 01:11:09,293
There's no Hi-Tec-C pen. They were the best.

1974
01:11:09,593 --> 01:11:10,792
Oh, that pen brand?

1975
01:11:10,793 --> 01:11:12,363
- That's right. - I know.

1976
01:11:12,663 --> 01:11:13,932
It was a luxury.

1977
01:11:13,933 --> 01:11:15,932
If scary kids asked to let them borrow Hi-Tec-C pens,

1978
01:11:15,933 --> 01:11:17,062
I was really anxious...

1979
01:11:17,063 --> 01:11:18,232
- that they wouldn't return them. - That's because...

1980
01:11:18,233 --> 01:11:19,472
if you drop it,

1981
01:11:19,473 --> 01:11:21,842
the tip of the pen would go in, and you can no longer use it.

1982
01:11:21,843 --> 01:11:24,002
- That's right. - Right. You mean the tip.

1983
01:11:24,003 --> 01:11:25,142
- Gosh, seriously. - Those who were good...

1984
01:11:25,143 --> 01:11:26,273
at note-taking used that brand a lot.

1985
01:11:26,513 --> 01:11:28,912
The finer the tip, the more popular it was.

1986
01:11:28,913 --> 01:11:30,043
- Really? - Yes.

1987
01:11:31,383 --> 01:11:33,653
(Staring)

1988
01:11:34,113 --> 01:11:36,583
(They busily look around.)

1989
01:11:36,753 --> 01:11:38,492
She scans them while walking as well.

1990
01:11:38,493 --> 01:11:39,892
(She scans them while walking as well.)

1991
01:11:39,893 --> 01:11:40,992
- She keeps scanning. - Of course.

1992
01:11:40,993 --> 01:11:42,122
She loves them.

1993
01:11:42,123 --> 01:11:43,592
She scans them while walking to the counter.

1994
01:11:43,593 --> 01:11:44,863
Of course.

1995
01:11:45,693 --> 01:11:48,063
Oh, we pay here? It's a self-checkout?

1996
01:11:50,033 --> 01:11:51,033
(The son checks them out at the self-checkout.)

1997
01:11:51,034 --> 01:11:52,103
That's right.

1998
01:11:53,803 --> 01:11:55,273
- Use my card. - No, I'll pay.

1999
01:11:55,443 --> 01:11:57,242
- Really? Here. - Of course.

2000
01:11:57,243 --> 01:11:58,272
(She's proud of him.)

2001
01:11:58,273 --> 01:11:59,943
It's best to use the son's card.

2002
01:12:00,343 --> 01:12:01,983
I'm confident in writing a journal in it.

2003
01:12:02,443 --> 01:12:03,882
- I'm sure you can. - Yes.

2004
01:12:03,883 --> 01:12:05,353
It's really thick.

2005
01:12:05,753 --> 01:12:07,913
I should get some albums if they have them here.

2006
01:12:09,153 --> 01:12:11,153
(Looking around)

2007
01:12:11,653 --> 01:12:13,193
This must be it.

2008
01:12:14,853 --> 01:12:15,963
Is this it?

2009
01:12:18,233 --> 01:12:19,692
The section where they sell music albums...

2010
01:12:19,693 --> 01:12:23,003
- got a lot smaller. - People don't use them a lot now.

2011
01:12:23,763 --> 01:12:25,802
Gosh, the section for music albums...

2012
01:12:25,803 --> 01:12:27,833
- got a lot smaller. - It's a lot smaller, right?

2013
01:12:28,843 --> 01:12:30,243
This is my album too.

2014
01:12:31,613 --> 01:12:32,913
This one was released last time.

2015
01:12:34,013 --> 01:12:35,213
Where is the recent one?

2016
01:12:36,583 --> 01:12:38,043
They have the old ones.

2017
01:12:39,153 --> 01:12:40,483
- They must be sold out. - Yes.

2018
01:12:40,683 --> 01:12:42,322
Singers can check their own albums...

2019
01:12:42,323 --> 01:12:43,953
- if they go there. - That's right.

2020
01:12:44,483 --> 01:12:46,692
Do you have my album, "HUNTER?"

2021
01:12:46,693 --> 01:12:47,823
It's over there.

2022
01:12:48,323 --> 01:12:49,692
Oh, it's at the front?

2023
01:12:49,693 --> 01:12:50,923
Mom, it's at the front.

2024
01:12:51,593 --> 01:12:53,633
(Brightening up)

2025
01:12:54,263 --> 01:12:55,702
(Turns out KEY's album was displayed separately.)

2026
01:12:55,703 --> 01:12:56,862
You have a separate section.

2027
01:12:56,863 --> 01:12:58,473
My goodness!

2028
01:12:58,833 --> 01:13:00,732
- How nice for singers. - Look at this!

2029
01:13:00,733 --> 01:13:03,603
Mine was new, so they displayed it at the front.

2030
01:13:03,873 --> 01:13:05,742
You're totally in the center.

2031
01:13:05,743 --> 01:13:08,383
- Gosh, it's selling well. - I'm so proud of you.

2032
01:13:09,283 --> 01:13:12,052
I punched in the wrong address, so it went to your place.

2033
01:13:12,053 --> 01:13:13,453
