2034
01:13:14,053 --> 01:13:15,883
I told her to get a new one while we were there.

2035
01:13:15,983 --> 01:13:17,123
- I see. - Get this.

2036
01:13:17,453 --> 01:13:19,952
It wouldn't feel so tense if there were too many displays.

2037
01:13:19,953 --> 01:13:21,793
- Right. It should be empty. - Yes, a little.

2038
01:13:21,893 --> 01:13:22,893
(Taking some away as though there are only a few left)

2039
01:13:22,894 --> 01:13:24,622
- That's right. - You should display them like that.

2040
01:13:24,623 --> 01:13:26,233
- As though it was selling well? - Of course.

2041
01:13:26,293 --> 01:13:27,933
Like they fell while people were grabbing them.

2042
01:13:28,503 --> 01:13:29,603
- Leave that. - Like this.

2043
01:13:32,133 --> 01:13:33,702
Does your mom buy your album with her money...

2044
01:13:33,703 --> 01:13:35,273
every time you release one?

2045
01:13:35,473 --> 01:13:37,042
She does.

2046
01:13:37,043 --> 01:13:39,712
- She buys ones for her friends too. - Really?

2047
01:13:39,713 --> 01:13:42,113
She gets some to keep for herself. One to open,

2048
01:13:42,343 --> 01:13:44,312
- and one to keep. - For collection.

2049
01:13:44,313 --> 01:13:45,412
- She buys them every time. - She could ask you.

2050
01:13:45,413 --> 01:13:48,113
I used to place the cartoons that I drew...

2051
01:13:48,653 --> 01:13:51,083
between books in the bookstore in my neighborhood.

2052
01:13:51,323 --> 01:13:53,693
I'd go and see if they were sold after school.

2053
01:13:54,023 --> 01:13:55,293
The thought itself is cute.

2054
01:13:55,523 --> 01:13:56,592
What price did you write on?

2055
01:13:56,593 --> 01:13:58,792
Similar to other items.

2056
01:13:58,793 --> 01:14:01,032
I set the price at 2.5 dollars.

2057
01:14:01,033 --> 01:14:02,962
I'd draw cartoons in my drawing book and place them.

2058
01:14:02,963 --> 01:14:04,903
You wanted to see if they'd be sold.

2059
01:14:06,003 --> 01:14:07,333
That'd be pricey now.

2060
01:14:08,033 --> 01:14:09,072
It'd be amazing...

2061
01:14:09,073 --> 01:14:10,143
- if you have the first edition. - If you have it...

2062
01:14:10,303 --> 01:14:12,773
That's a novel idea, though.

2063
01:14:13,513 --> 01:14:15,942
We have photo cards that we give out.

2064
01:14:15,943 --> 01:14:17,083
Photo cards?

2065
01:14:17,913 --> 01:14:19,153
You should get them.

2066
01:14:20,053 --> 01:14:21,182
- They didn't leave them out. - Thank you.

2067
01:14:21,183 --> 01:14:23,023
- Thank you. - Thank you.

2068
01:14:23,523 --> 01:14:24,583
Have a good day.

2069
01:14:25,353 --> 01:14:26,793
Let's go.

2070
01:14:27,293 --> 01:14:28,563
They made the most of their time.

2071
01:14:29,663 --> 01:14:31,562
You look like you lost more weight.

2072
01:14:31,563 --> 01:14:32,793
Your skin looks fairer.

2073
01:14:36,463 --> 01:14:38,502
- Come on in. - Home sweet home.

2074
01:14:38,503 --> 01:14:40,773
(Home sweet home)

2075
01:14:41,773 --> 01:14:44,743
- Son, it's been really long. - I'm home.

2076
01:14:45,073 --> 01:14:46,912
Last time you came was December last year.

2077
01:14:46,913 --> 01:14:49,243
- Mom, take this. - It's been more than six months.

2078
01:14:49,613 --> 01:14:51,683
It's really not easy to go to your parents' in another city.

2079
01:14:52,213 --> 01:14:54,853
I'll go get changed. You should get some rest too.

2080
01:14:55,823 --> 01:14:57,353
(Yawning)

2081
01:14:57,823 --> 01:14:59,752
You yawn automatically when you're at your parent's, right?

2082
01:14:59,753 --> 01:15:01,053
- You get sleepy. - Yes.

2083
01:15:09,433 --> 01:15:10,503
Goodness.

2084
01:15:14,503 --> 01:15:15,573
My gosh.

2085
01:15:17,203 --> 01:15:18,203
(Groaning)

2086
01:15:19,413 --> 01:15:21,173
(Grunting)

2087
01:15:21,983 --> 01:15:25,152
You drove there and walked around the whole day.

2088
01:15:25,153 --> 01:15:26,313
You must've been tired.

2089
01:15:27,383 --> 01:15:31,123
(He puts away the stuff he chose with his mom.)

2090
01:15:34,453 --> 01:15:35,462
(Flopping)

2091
01:15:35,463 --> 01:15:37,393
If you sleep now, your day could get messed up.

2092
01:15:38,163 --> 01:15:40,463
Your bed at your parents' makes you sleepy.

2093
01:15:40,993 --> 01:15:42,932
She changed the blanket for me to fit the season.

2094
01:15:42,933 --> 01:15:44,033
Oh, my.

2095
01:15:46,233 --> 01:15:48,672
(Tossing and turning)

2096
01:15:48,673 --> 01:15:49,743
He must be sleepy.

2097
01:15:52,273 --> 01:15:54,643
At 11pm, you'd fight with them about you staying or leaving.

2098
01:15:54,773 --> 01:15:56,143
Right. "I'm leaving."

2099
01:15:56,743 --> 01:15:58,652
- "No, it's late. It's dangerous." - That's right.

2100
01:15:58,653 --> 01:16:00,052
"It's not dangerous. I'm not a kid."

2101
01:16:00,053 --> 01:16:01,353
"Yes, you are."

2102
01:16:02,053 --> 01:16:03,253
Are you two writing a script?

2103
01:16:04,323 --> 01:16:06,652
- This is the repertoire. - It really is.

2104
01:16:06,653 --> 01:16:09,122
There are street lights everywhere even if I leave at night.

2105
01:16:09,123 --> 01:16:10,422
- The roads are well-paved too. - Of course.

2106
01:16:10,423 --> 01:16:12,032
"It's dangerous. It's too dark."

2107
01:16:12,033 --> 01:16:13,232
Of course it's dark. It's night.

2108
01:16:13,233 --> 01:16:15,403
- "Sleep over." - Driving is always dangerous.

2109
01:16:15,663 --> 01:16:17,403
I sleep over if I can.

2110
01:16:17,663 --> 01:16:19,072
Daegu is too far too.

2111
01:16:19,073 --> 01:16:20,573
- You should sleep over. - It's far. I should sleep over.

2112
01:16:21,603 --> 01:16:23,503
(Soon, he gets wrapped in comfort that his parent's place gives...)

2113
01:16:24,403 --> 01:16:26,272
(and sleeps soundly.)

2114
01:16:26,273 --> 01:16:27,613
Ki Bum.

2115
01:16:28,883 --> 01:16:31,483
(Getting up)

2116
01:16:32,353 --> 01:16:34,752
- Gosh, I passed out. - Come on out and eat.

2117
01:16:34,753 --> 01:16:36,223
- Indeed, moms are amazing. - Okay.

2118
01:16:38,753 --> 01:16:40,152
Come on out, Ki Bum.

2119
01:16:40,153 --> 01:16:41,153
(Let's eat, Son.)

2120
01:16:41,593 --> 01:16:43,893
That's the alarm. My mom's alarm.

2121
01:16:45,463 --> 01:16:47,533
I napped like I passed out.

2122
01:16:48,603 --> 01:16:49,663
You must be tired.

2123
01:16:50,203 --> 01:16:51,663
Your mom doesn't cook, though.

2124
01:16:51,803 --> 01:16:52,903
Did she buy them?

2125
01:16:54,131 --> 01:16:57,101
I napped like I passed out.

2126
01:16:57,901 --> 01:16:59,131
You must be tired.

2127
01:17:00,531 --> 01:17:02,170
Your mom doesn't cook, though.

2128
01:17:02,171 --> 01:17:03,241
Did she buy them?

2129
01:17:03,971 --> 01:17:05,341
It's been so long.

2130
01:17:05,771 --> 01:17:07,771
- You got a cake too? - Gosh, 34.

2131
01:17:08,441 --> 01:17:10,141
(Touched)

2132
01:17:16,451 --> 01:17:17,481
(Blowing)

2133
01:17:17,751 --> 01:17:18,850
(Happy birthday, son.)

2134
01:17:18,851 --> 01:17:20,790
Mom, it's been so long since we last did it.

2135
01:17:20,791 --> 01:17:21,921
I know.

2136
01:17:22,621 --> 01:17:24,090
I got you a gift too.

2137
01:17:24,091 --> 01:17:25,091
- Gosh. - Yes!

2138
01:17:25,092 --> 01:17:26,790
A gift from Mom and Dad.

2139
01:17:26,791 --> 01:17:29,060
We couldn't pick one as you're all grown up.

2140
01:17:29,061 --> 01:17:30,830
- Cash. - It's pocket money.

2141
01:17:30,831 --> 01:17:32,600
A letter from your dad.

2142
01:17:32,601 --> 01:17:33,770
Dad wrote me a letter?

2143
01:17:33,771 --> 01:17:35,071
- A letter from your dad? - Of course.

2144
01:17:35,741 --> 01:17:37,541
Your dad wrote a letter.

2145
01:17:37,841 --> 01:17:39,241
Gosh, this is amazing.

2146
01:17:40,011 --> 01:17:41,070
(Seeing you pull off such a difficult choreography...)

2147
01:17:41,071 --> 01:17:42,140
(in your early 20s, it got me worried about your joints.)

2148
01:17:42,141 --> 01:17:43,381
He always types it.

2149
01:17:43,581 --> 01:17:45,411
I almost asked him to release his font.

2150
01:17:46,511 --> 01:17:48,381
On my birthday, they'd always write a letter...

2151
01:17:48,781 --> 01:17:50,720
and withdraw new bills from the bank.

2152
01:17:50,721 --> 01:17:52,250
- Really? - For pocket money.

2153
01:17:52,251 --> 01:17:55,090
"Even if you make money, someone needs to take care of you."

2154
01:17:55,091 --> 01:17:57,121
- They'd always do this. - Yes.

2155
01:17:57,191 --> 01:17:58,831
There's a pleasure in the feel of cash.

2156
01:17:59,831 --> 01:18:01,690
He wrote it in Daejeon and dropped it by here.

2157
01:18:01,691 --> 01:18:03,100
- Really? - Yes.

2158
01:18:03,101 --> 01:18:04,601
My dad works in Daejeon.

2159
01:18:06,531 --> 01:18:08,100
(Checking)

2160
01:18:08,101 --> 01:18:09,400
- They gave you a lot. - That's a lot of money.

2161
01:18:09,401 --> 01:18:10,470
I think there's about 1,000 dollars.

2162
01:18:10,471 --> 01:18:12,011
- I'll use it well. - Okay.

2163
01:18:12,041 --> 01:18:13,670
Regardless of me making money,

2164
01:18:13,671 --> 01:18:15,211
it makes me happy.

2165
01:18:15,311 --> 01:18:16,411
That's right.

2166
01:18:17,341 --> 01:18:19,950
All right, I made the bone soup...

2167
01:18:19,951 --> 01:18:21,550
that you miss.

2168
01:18:21,551 --> 01:18:24,821
I made the bone soup that you miss.

2169
01:18:24,921 --> 01:18:27,351
To celebrate the holiday...

2170
01:18:27,721 --> 01:18:29,020
- You made it? - and your birthday.

2171
01:18:29,021 --> 01:18:31,020
Yes, I made it.

2172
01:18:31,021 --> 01:18:33,031
You know how hard it is to make bone soup, right?

2173
01:18:34,391 --> 01:18:36,461
(4 years ago, she made seaweed soup for him.)

2174
01:18:37,061 --> 01:18:38,401
It's too bland.

2175
01:18:39,031 --> 01:18:40,830
(His mom wasn't interested in cooking much...)

2176
01:18:40,831 --> 01:18:42,600
(because she was busy working.)

2177
01:18:42,601 --> 01:18:44,571
KEY cooks better than his mom.

2178
01:18:45,411 --> 01:18:47,741
I did my best to make it.

2179
01:18:47,871 --> 01:18:49,440
I got up at 4am for it.

2180
01:18:49,441 --> 01:18:51,411
It took five hours to drain the blood.

2181
01:18:52,981 --> 01:18:54,310
She must've gone through a lot.

2182
01:18:54,311 --> 01:18:57,881
(She got up early in the morning and worked hard.)

2183
01:18:58,691 --> 01:19:00,150
(She put in a lot of effort for a long time...)

2184
01:19:00,151 --> 01:19:01,620
(for his son who'd love the soup.)

2185
01:19:01,621 --> 01:19:03,390
You must have tripe in the bone soup.

2186
01:19:03,391 --> 01:19:04,491
Yes.

2187
01:19:04,521 --> 01:19:06,130
You must have tripe in the bone soup.

2188
01:19:06,131 --> 01:19:08,060
- Tripe? As in cow stomachs? - Yes.

2189
01:19:08,061 --> 01:19:09,700
Yes, tripe.

2190
01:19:09,701 --> 01:19:12,131
- Tripes are really hard to handle. - You're right.

2191
01:19:12,401 --> 01:19:15,170
There aren't many places that sell tripes because it's summer.

2192
01:19:15,171 --> 01:19:18,971
So I went to the butcher's in front of the slaughterhouse...

2193
01:19:19,141 --> 01:19:21,171
in Geumdan-dong.

2194
01:19:21,611 --> 01:19:23,211
(Surprised)

2195
01:19:23,811 --> 01:19:25,351
Oh, it's made with lamb?

2196
01:19:25,611 --> 01:19:27,280
No, the cow stomach.

2197
01:19:27,281 --> 01:19:28,881
No, the cow stomach.

2198
01:19:29,281 --> 01:19:31,220
- Oh, it's not made with lamb? - No.

2199
01:19:31,221 --> 01:19:32,521
Are you from Mongolia?

2200
01:19:32,891 --> 01:19:33,920
The cow stomach.

2201
01:19:33,921 --> 01:19:35,661
- Stomach? - His grandma isn't from Mongolia.

2202
01:19:36,161 --> 01:19:38,260
- The cow stomach is called tripe. - As in beef tripe.

2203
01:19:38,261 --> 01:19:40,291
- We call them beef tripe. - Oh, the thing...

2204
01:19:40,491 --> 01:19:42,260
I thought it was lamb.

2205
01:19:42,261 --> 01:19:43,831
There are many people who don't know that.

2206
01:19:43,931 --> 01:19:45,470
Many people don't get it either.

2207
01:19:45,471 --> 01:19:46,570
You know, like beef omasum.

2208
01:19:46,571 --> 01:19:48,371
Cows have four stomachs.

2209
01:19:48,971 --> 01:19:50,471
There are so many things to learn.

2210
01:19:51,441 --> 01:19:53,210
You made Grandma's soup?

2211
01:19:53,211 --> 01:19:55,070
- That's right. - I've really wanted to eat this.

2212
01:19:55,071 --> 01:19:57,180
They don't sell this anywhere.

2213
01:19:57,181 --> 01:19:58,380
They don't.

2214
01:19:58,381 --> 01:20:01,150
It's really hard to get tripes these days

2215
01:20:01,151 --> 01:20:02,420
Really? They're hard to get?

2216
01:20:02,421 --> 01:20:03,950
It's hard to get fresh tripes.

2217
01:20:03,951 --> 01:20:04,951
They have a gamey smell.

2218
01:20:04,952 --> 01:20:07,020
I was really surprised to see the beef bone soup.

2219
01:20:07,021 --> 01:20:08,621
It's really time-consuming.

2220
01:20:08,961 --> 01:20:10,291
It's my grandma's recipe.

2221
01:20:10,461 --> 01:20:13,531
Bone soup, braised crab in soy sauce.

2222
01:20:13,831 --> 01:20:16,101
It's braised crab in soy sauce.

2223
01:20:16,301 --> 01:20:17,560
- Crab soup. - There were a few dishes...

2224
01:20:17,561 --> 01:20:18,870
that I liked.

2225
01:20:18,871 --> 01:20:20,300
(Grandma's dishes that KEY used to love)

2226
01:20:20,301 --> 01:20:21,770
There are days...

2227
01:20:21,771 --> 01:20:24,770
when I don't crave anything.

2228
01:20:24,771 --> 01:20:26,771
But I always want that dish.

2229
01:20:27,541 --> 01:20:29,181
- Always. - There are dishes like that.

2230
01:20:29,341 --> 01:20:31,280
I always craved it ever since I was young.

2231
01:20:31,281 --> 01:20:32,751
I always liked it constantly.

2232
01:20:34,111 --> 01:20:36,151
(Grandma's bone soup that his mom made)

2233
01:20:36,851 --> 01:20:38,220
Try the soup first...

2234
01:20:38,221 --> 01:20:39,451
- Thank you for the food. - and see if it tastes the same.

2235
01:20:40,691 --> 01:20:43,791
(Carefully taking the first sip)

2236
01:20:44,521 --> 01:20:46,361
(We're curious.)

2237
01:20:47,561 --> 01:20:48,631
(Exclaiming)

2238
01:20:48,961 --> 01:20:51,931
- Gosh, it's good. - Does it have the same taste?

2239
01:20:53,901 --> 01:20:55,801
It's so good.

2240
01:20:56,201 --> 01:20:58,541
It was the same taste as the one Grandma made.

2241
01:20:59,241 --> 01:21:00,941
This is...

2242
01:21:01,241 --> 01:21:03,981
not the kind of soup you can have...

2243
01:21:04,181 --> 01:21:05,480
in just any bone soup restaurant.

2244
01:21:05,481 --> 01:21:06,680
It's a little different.

2245
01:21:06,681 --> 01:21:07,951
- The taste. - It's totally different.

2246
01:21:07,981 --> 01:21:09,221
It was so good.

2247
01:21:09,251 --> 01:21:10,980
I can tell how serious you were.

2248
01:21:10,981 --> 01:21:12,521
- I can tell from here. - It was so good.

2249
01:21:12,991 --> 01:21:15,261
- It's so good. - Right? I like it too.

2250
01:21:17,591 --> 01:21:18,631
I'm glad.

2251
01:21:19,291 --> 01:21:21,591
It was worth all the trouble seeing how you eat so well.

2252
01:21:21,631 --> 01:21:23,131
Your mom is really happy too.

2253
01:21:26,831 --> 01:21:28,501
I used to love tripes.

2254
01:21:29,041 --> 01:21:30,970
Yes, you did. You said you couldn't call it bone soup...

2255
01:21:30,971 --> 01:21:32,311
- if it didn't have tripes. - That's right.

2256
01:21:32,871 --> 01:21:34,440
- That's the one. - Oh, that?

2257
01:21:34,441 --> 01:21:35,781
That's right. That's the one.

2258
01:21:36,241 --> 01:21:37,411
Does it taste similar?

2259
01:21:37,581 --> 01:21:39,551
Yes! It's so good.

2260
01:21:40,251 --> 01:21:42,251
- It was exactly like this. - Yes.

2261
01:21:44,251 --> 01:21:46,351
(Thanks to his mom, he got to enjoy the taste he missed.)

2262
01:21:47,051 --> 01:21:48,190
It's good.

2263
01:21:48,191 --> 01:21:49,391
Ki Bum is eating so well.

2264
01:21:49,821 --> 01:21:52,090
I was worried that it wouldn't taste the same.

2265
01:21:52,091 --> 01:21:53,091
(Worried that it wouldn't taste like his grandma's dish)

2266
01:21:53,261 --> 01:21:55,130
If it tastes the same to you,

2267
01:21:55,131 --> 01:21:57,101
that means it'd taste the same to me too.

2268
01:21:58,001 --> 01:21:59,730
Still, you'd remember it the best.

2269
01:21:59,731 --> 01:22:02,071
Right, because I used to love it.

2270
01:22:02,341 --> 01:22:04,200
It's nice that it tastes the same.

2271
01:22:04,201 --> 01:22:05,271
I know.

2272
01:22:06,511 --> 01:22:07,711
I'm having this...

2273
01:22:08,611 --> 01:22:10,211
after around 13 years.

2274
01:22:10,711 --> 01:22:12,910
I still have the last batch that Grandma made.

2275
01:22:12,911 --> 01:22:13,951
What?

2276
01:22:14,011 --> 01:22:15,150
- You still do? - In the freezer.

2277
01:22:15,151 --> 01:22:16,350
Oh, you froze it.

2278
01:22:16,351 --> 01:22:17,721
I can't have it now.

2279
01:22:18,081 --> 01:22:19,521
You can't.

2280
01:22:20,521 --> 01:22:23,520
The last bone soup Grandma made before she passed...

2281
01:22:23,521 --> 01:22:26,260
is still in my freezer.

2282
01:22:26,261 --> 01:22:27,991
I couldn't eat it.

2283
01:22:28,491 --> 01:22:30,731
It's never been thawed for 13 years.

2284
01:22:32,001 --> 01:22:34,301
I always brought it with me whenever I moved.

2285
01:22:35,071 --> 01:22:36,700
You couldn't throw it away.

2286
01:22:36,701 --> 01:22:38,671
- I could never throw it out. - Of course not.

2287
01:22:39,311 --> 01:22:41,171
Give it to me. I can try it.

2288
01:22:42,511 --> 01:22:44,380
- That... - He's a frozen food expert.

2289
01:22:44,381 --> 01:22:46,010
Wait. I don't think he should eat that.

2290
01:22:46,011 --> 01:22:47,981
- I'll do a review on it. - Kian84, that's...

2291
01:22:48,081 --> 01:22:50,080
You'll get sick even if you're Elsa.

2292
01:22:50,081 --> 01:22:52,791
Let's have it on the field day.

2293
01:22:53,051 --> 01:22:54,890
- On the field day? - Seriously...

2294
01:22:54,891 --> 01:22:56,190
Make a whole pot of it on the field day.

2295
01:22:56,191 --> 01:22:57,361
It's a festival.

2296
01:22:57,461 --> 01:23:00,091
It's really precious, but if you actually eat it,

2297
01:23:00,131 --> 01:23:02,761
you might be able to see Ki Bum's grandma.

2298
01:23:03,231 --> 01:23:04,830
That's what we're worried about.

2299
01:23:04,831 --> 01:23:06,930
- "Hurry here." - We should say hello.

2300
01:23:06,931 --> 01:23:08,570
- You should. - "Hurry here."

2301
01:23:08,571 --> 01:23:10,571
- I'm good with the elderly. - Sure.

2302
01:23:11,601 --> 01:23:13,841
She probably knows that I couldn't eat it...

2303
01:23:14,041 --> 01:23:16,781
not even once after Grandma passed.

2304
01:23:16,941 --> 01:23:19,351
That's like my grandma's aged kimchi.

2305
01:23:19,711 --> 01:23:21,710
Also, I told her a few times in passing...

2306
01:23:21,711 --> 01:23:22,980
that I want to eat it,

2307
01:23:22,981 --> 01:23:25,151
but no restaurants have bone soups that taste like hers.

2308
01:23:25,351 --> 01:23:27,550
It was really good. I haven't felt that in a long time.

2309
01:23:27,551 --> 01:23:28,760
(Thanks to Mom, I could taste it again.)

2310
01:23:28,761 --> 01:23:30,891
Is it different from the regular bone soup?

2311
01:23:30,961 --> 01:23:32,961
As for my grandma,

2312
01:23:33,091 --> 01:23:34,660
she drains the blood for hours.

2313
01:23:34,661 --> 01:23:36,731
She throws out the soup she boils for the first time.

2314
01:23:37,001 --> 01:23:38,100
She throws out the second batch too.

2315
01:23:38,101 --> 01:23:39,330
So it's really time-consuming.

2316
01:23:39,331 --> 01:23:40,700
The ones with a lot of intestines...

2317
01:23:40,701 --> 01:23:42,170
- are usually spicy. - That's right.

2318
01:23:42,171 --> 01:23:43,871
- Because of the smell. - It's because of the smell.

2319
01:23:43,971 --> 01:23:46,970
She used really nice tripes,

2320
01:23:46,971 --> 01:23:48,511
which added a nutty flavor.

2321
01:23:48,571 --> 01:23:49,740
- The nutty flavor from meat. - The intestines...

2322
01:23:49,741 --> 01:23:50,840
The nutty flavor from the intestines...

2323
01:23:50,841 --> 01:23:51,941
- is added. - I wonder what that tastes like.

2324
01:23:52,111 --> 01:23:53,681
I want to try it.

2325
01:23:55,481 --> 01:23:56,950
(Gulping down)

2326
01:23:56,951 --> 01:23:57,980
- You need to drink that... - That's it.

2327
01:23:57,981 --> 01:23:58,990
Instead of using a spoon.

2328
01:23:58,991 --> 01:24:00,521
- It's like medicine. - It's like medicine.

2329
01:24:02,621 --> 01:24:04,861
(Grandma's bone soup is like tonic.)

2330
01:24:05,161 --> 01:24:06,531
Grandma must be happy.

2331
01:24:08,691 --> 01:24:10,200
(Yes, this hits the spot.)

2332
01:24:10,201 --> 01:24:11,261
It must be delicious.

2333
01:24:11,631 --> 01:24:13,270
Since you were at it,

2334
01:24:13,271 --> 01:24:15,031
you should've made this much like Grandma used to.

2335
01:24:15,431 --> 01:24:16,440
I did.

2336
01:24:16,441 --> 01:24:18,370
- You did? - I froze some.

2337
01:24:18,371 --> 01:24:19,610
You can take them.

2338
01:24:19,611 --> 01:24:21,540
Yes, there was a reason why she made a lot.

2339
01:24:21,541 --> 01:24:23,311
Didn't your moms...

2340
01:24:23,441 --> 01:24:25,550
feed you bone soup for a month...

2341
01:24:25,551 --> 01:24:26,710
once she made it?

2342
01:24:26,711 --> 01:24:28,050
- Of course. - She made a whole pot.

2343
01:24:28,051 --> 01:24:30,150
- They'd use a huge steaming pot. - I used to have it a lot.

2344
01:24:30,151 --> 01:24:32,120
- Right? - Before going to school,

2345
01:24:32,121 --> 01:24:33,650
- she added rice and fed me. - You had to finish it.

2346
01:24:33,651 --> 01:24:34,791
That's right.

2347
01:24:34,851 --> 01:24:36,090
She told me to have the soup, at least.

2348
01:24:36,091 --> 01:24:37,790
- Yes. That's right. - That's right.

2349
01:24:37,791 --> 01:24:38,830
- She'd tell us to drink it. - That's right.

2350
01:24:38,831 --> 01:24:40,491
I used to be really skinny.

2351
01:24:40,531 --> 01:24:41,890
After having that,

2352
01:24:41,891 --> 01:24:43,330
- Come on. - I gained weight.

2353
01:24:43,331 --> 01:24:44,860
- Don't be ridiculous. - No, when I was a baby.

2354
01:24:44,861 --> 01:24:46,800
Who's not skinny when they're a baby?

2355
01:24:46,801 --> 01:24:48,270
You seem to lie well.

2356
01:24:48,271 --> 01:24:50,600
Everyone was skinny when they were a baby.

2357
01:24:50,601 --> 01:24:51,971
I was skinny.

2358
01:24:52,171 --> 01:24:53,710
But they said having bone soup...

2359
01:24:53,711 --> 01:24:55,410
would give you an appetite.

2360
01:24:55,411 --> 01:24:57,441
- Since then, I have gained weight. - How many tons of it did you have?

2361
01:24:58,511 --> 01:24:59,880
Bone soup gave you an appetite.

2362
01:24:59,881 --> 01:25:01,281
I got an appetite when I was young.

2363
01:25:01,451 --> 01:25:02,520
You got a lot of appetite.

2364
01:25:02,521 --> 01:25:03,681
I did.

2365
01:25:04,621 --> 01:25:05,690
Try the radish kimchi.

2366
01:25:05,691 --> 01:25:07,491
I made this radish kimchi.

2367
01:25:07,821 --> 01:25:09,221
It's not store-bought?

2368
01:25:09,391 --> 01:25:11,760
No, I made this.

2369
01:25:11,761 --> 01:25:14,090
To have with the bone soup.

2370
01:25:14,091 --> 01:25:15,730
So this is the only thing from the department store?

2371
01:25:15,731 --> 01:25:17,560
No, I made this too.

2372
01:25:17,561 --> 01:25:18,561
All of it?

2373
01:25:18,562 --> 01:25:20,330
Mom can do this much.

2374
01:25:20,331 --> 01:25:21,331
Really?

2375
01:25:21,332 --> 01:25:23,641
It was the first time Mom made every dish.

2376
01:25:23,741 --> 01:25:24,770
Now that she has time.

2377
01:25:24,771 --> 01:25:25,911
She has more time on her hands.

2378
01:25:26,171 --> 01:25:28,171
I learned a special recipe.

2379
01:25:30,511 --> 01:25:33,351
Radishes like this aren't sweet.

2380
01:25:33,781 --> 01:25:36,120
So, you need to add this bit of MSG.

2381
01:25:36,121 --> 01:25:37,720
- Yes, you must. - You need to add it.

2382
01:25:37,721 --> 01:25:40,020
It looked like she was finding cooking fun.

2383
01:25:40,021 --> 01:25:41,151
You're right.

2384
01:25:42,991 --> 01:25:46,531
(Mom, you're the best. This is so good.)

2385
01:25:47,631 --> 01:25:49,531
Actually, to me,

2386
01:25:49,701 --> 01:25:51,830
it was the day I was born.

2387
01:25:51,831 --> 01:25:53,471
Just that, no more or less.

2388
01:25:53,831 --> 01:25:55,770
Just because something sad happened,

2389
01:25:55,771 --> 01:25:57,141
I didn't want to be too down.

2390
01:25:57,241 --> 01:26:00,041
I'd rather remind myself of the things I was grateful for.

2391
01:26:00,071 --> 01:26:02,170
It's a day for me to recharge and reset...

2392
01:26:02,171 --> 01:26:04,380
to move forward.

2393
01:26:04,381 --> 01:26:06,411
That's how my birthday would be.

2394
01:26:07,711 --> 01:26:09,581
I'm so happy that you're eating so well.

2395
01:26:09,951 --> 01:26:11,351
This is really...

2396
01:26:12,591 --> 01:26:13,921
It feels like I'm traveling through time.

2397
01:26:15,451 --> 01:26:17,861
It means so much to me.

2398
01:26:18,321 --> 01:26:20,261
- I'm full. - Seriously.

2399
01:26:22,401 --> 01:26:26,031
The strength that food gives you is really big.

2400
01:26:26,271 --> 01:26:27,801
(Next story)

2401
01:26:28,801 --> 01:26:30,541
(She's back here after a long time.)

2402
01:26:32,311 --> 01:26:35,170
(She takes a step...)

2403
01:26:35,171 --> 01:26:36,241
(and plops down.)

2404
01:26:36,611 --> 01:26:37,940
Gosh, this is so hard.

2405
01:26:37,941 --> 01:26:40,651
(The house she entered with much difficulty)

2406
01:26:41,681 --> 01:26:43,921
(Grandma, Grandpa, Na Rae is here.)

2407
01:26:44,881 --> 01:26:47,550
(After both of them passed, )

2408
01:26:47,551 --> 01:26:48,921
(the house became empty.)

2409
01:26:49,861 --> 01:26:52,361
(Na Rae made up her mind to clean up the house.)

2410
01:26:53,631 --> 01:26:56,231
(It tortured me the moment I opened the gate.)

2411
01:26:57,861 --> 01:26:59,030
(Na Rae)

2412
01:26:59,031 --> 01:27:01,271
(We're here!)

2413
01:27:03,001 --> 01:27:05,001
(Why are you crying by yourself?)

2414
01:27:06,171 --> 01:27:08,510
(Trust us.)

2415
01:27:08,511 --> 01:27:10,080
It won't be easy to pluck them out.

2416
01:27:10,081 --> 01:27:11,910
(A bunch of weeds)

2417
01:27:11,911 --> 01:27:13,581
(Lifting with no problem)

2418
01:27:14,451 --> 01:27:16,051
(Continuing to work without hesitation)

2419
01:27:17,151 --> 01:27:19,551
(Kian84 is the head farmhand.)

2420
01:27:23,391 --> 01:27:25,761
(Moorincess only makes so much noise.)

2421
01:27:26,831 --> 01:27:27,831
(Clank)

2422
01:27:28,591 --> 01:27:29,601
(Studying the room)

2423
01:27:30,331 --> 01:27:31,861
(It's okay. Let's have coffee.)

2424
01:27:32,531 --> 01:27:33,971
(Sworn brotherhood)

2425
01:27:35,301 --> 01:27:37,571
(Strengthening loyalty while washing each other's back)

2426
01:27:38,701 --> 01:27:40,211
(Gosh, this feels great.)

2427
01:27:41,111 --> 01:27:42,211
(Laughing with her friends, )

2428
01:27:42,741 --> 01:27:44,381
(the old feelings are washed away.)

2429
01:27:45,441 --> 01:27:47,581
(Back to Home Together with Sworn Brotherhood)

2430
01:27:48,481 --> 01:27:51,881
(An authority on the musical stage, Kai)

2431
01:27:53,021 --> 01:27:54,721
(Shall I become another version of myself?)

2432
01:27:56,691 --> 01:27:58,791
(He sets off with determination in his combat suit.)

2433
01:27:59,691 --> 01:28:00,861
(Opening)

2434
01:28:02,601 --> 01:28:04,801
(Another stage of mine where I'll pour out my passion)

2435
01:28:05,771 --> 01:28:07,131
(The professor's office is filled with his favorite things.)

2436
01:28:07,901 --> 01:28:09,241
(Professor mode, on)

2437
01:28:10,701 --> 01:28:12,641
(What's important is confidence in yourself.)

2438
01:28:13,371 --> 01:28:15,070
(Filled with confidence, )

2439
01:28:15,071 --> 01:28:16,911
(he delivers coffee?)

2440
01:28:17,681 --> 01:28:19,911
(I'm the youngest.)

2441
01:28:20,311 --> 01:28:21,311
(Have some coffee, my seniors.)

2442
01:28:21,751 --> 01:28:22,921
(Nerve-racking conference time for the professors)

2443
01:28:23,551 --> 01:28:25,150
(Yes...)

2444
01:28:25,151 --> 01:28:26,551
(Nodding automatically)

2445
01:28:26,921 --> 01:28:27,921
(What do you think about it?)

2446
01:28:29,061 --> 01:28:31,791
(I think it's great.)

2447
01:28:32,591 --> 01:28:33,730
(He goes to the canteen to regain strength.)

2448
01:28:33,731 --> 01:28:35,030
(Give me a lot, please.)

2449
01:28:35,031 --> 01:28:36,161
Thank you.

2450
01:28:37,031 --> 01:28:39,371
(Pork cutlet is perfect for the youngest.)

2451
01:28:39,471 --> 01:28:40,831
(Goodbye to the healthy meal for a while.)

2452
01:28:41,301 --> 01:28:42,941
(Inhaling like crazy)

2453
01:28:43,471 --> 01:28:45,470
(I, Who Was an Authority on Stage, )

2454
01:28:45,471 --> 01:28:48,271
(Am the Youngest in This World?)
